\p
\v 1 Then¦337397 Yahweh¦337400 \add ≈gave me¦337401 this\add* message¦337398:
\v 2 “Son¦337404 of¦337404 humanity¦337406, you¦337411 live¦337412 among a rebellious \add ≈people group\add* who¦337413 have eyes¦337414 to see¦337416, yet they¦337418 don't see¦337418, and who have ears¦337419 to hear¦337421, but¦337422 don't¦337422 listen¦337423,\x + \xo 12:2: \xt Isa 6:9-10; Jer 5:21; Mrk 8:18.\x* because¦337424 they're a¦337425 rebellious¦337426 \add ≈people group\add*.
\p
\v 3 “Therefore, son¦337430 of¦337430 humanity¦337432, \add ≈pack up your stuff ready¦337433 to¦337434 go¦337437 into¦337437\add* exile¦337437, and \add ≈each day¦337438 while they're watching\add*, start going¦337440 out \add somewhere\add*, because¦337449 \add ≈while they're watching\add*, I'll exile¦337440 you from¦337441 your place to another¦337445 place. Perhaps¦337447 they'll¦337448 begin to see¦337448, even though they're \add such\add* rebellious¦337451 \add ≈people\add*.
\v 4 \add ≈Each day¦337458 while they're watching,\add* bring¦337454 out¦337454 your¦337455 things for an exile¦337457, \add then\add* as they watch in¦337462 the evening¦337462, go¦337461 out¦337461 in the way that \add ≈people do\add* when going¦337464 into exile¦337465.
\v 5 Dig¦337468 a hole through the \add city\add* wall¦337471 \add ≈where they'll see you¦337472 do it\add*, and¦337472 go out¦337472 through it¦337473.
\v 6 \add ≈While they're watching\add*, lift¦337479 your things up¦337479 onto your shoulder¦337478, and bring¦337481 them out¦337481 in the darkness¦337480. Cover¦337483 your¦337482 face¦337482, because¦337489 you¦337485 mustn't see¦337485 \add &this¦337488\add* land¦337488, since¦337489 I've¦337492 \add ≈made¦337492 you¦337492 into¦337493\add* a¦337491 sign¦337491 for the¦337493 \add ≈Israeli¦337494 people\add*.”
\p
\v 7 \add ≈So¦337496\add* I¦337496 did¦337496 just¦337498 as¦337498 I¦337499 was¦337499 instructed¦337499: I¦337501 brought¦337501 my things for an exile¦337503 out in the daytime¦337504, and¦337505 in¦337505 the evening¦337505 I¦337506 dug¦337506 a hole through the wall¦337509 by¦337510 hand¦337510. I¦337512 brought¦337512 my things out¦337512 in the dark¦337511, and lifted¦337516 them up¦337516 onto \add &my¦337517\add* shoulder¦337515 \add ≈as they watched\add*.
\rem Need to make next verse style consistent throughout the document: Yahweh GAVE ME a message, vs Yahweh's message CAME TO ME.
\p
\v 8 ⇔The \add next\add* morning¦337525, Yahweh¦337523 \add ≈gave me this\add* message¦337521:
\v 9 “Son¦337528 of¦337528 humanity¦337530, haven't those rebellious¦337537 \add ≈Israeli¦337535 people\add* asked¦337532 you¦337533 what¦337538 you're¦337539 doing¦337540?
\v 10 Tell¦337542 them¦337543 that the master¦337546 Yahweh¦337547 says¦337545 this: ‘this prophetic action concerns the¦337548 ruler¦337548 in¦337551 Yerushalem¦337551 \add !(Jerusalem¦337551)\add* and¦337553 all¦337553 the¦337555 \add other\add* \add ≈Israeli¦337556 people\add* who¦337557 are¦337560 there.’
\v 11 Tell¦337562 them that \add %you're¦337563\add* a sign¦337564 to them, and that everything \add %you've\add* done¦337566 will¦337568 happen to¦337569 them¦337569—they'll¦337572 be \add ≈captured and taken into¦337570 exile¦337570\add* \add in another country\add*.
\v 12 \add ≈Their¦337577 leader¦337574\add* will¦337581 lift¦337581 his things up¦337581 onto \add &his\add* shoulder¦337580 in¦337582 the dark¦337582, and¦337583 will¦337583 go¦337583 out¦337583 through the wall¦337584. They'll¦337585 dig¦337585 through the wall and take¦337586 their things out¦337586. He'll¦337594 cover¦337589 his¦337588 face¦337588, so he won't¦337592 see¦337594 the¦337600 \add ≈place¦337600\add* \add he's leaving\add*.
\v 13 I'll¦337602 spread¦337602 my net out over him¦337606 and¦337607 he'll¦337607 be¦337607 caught¦337607 in¦337608 my¦337608 trap, then¦337609 I'll¦337609 take¦337609 him¦337610 \add away\add* to¦337611 Bavel¦337611 \add !(Babylon¦337611)\add* (the¦337612 land¦337612 of¦337612 the¦337613 Kasdim¦337613 \add !(Chaldeans¦337613)\add*), but¦337614 he¦337617 won't¦337615 see¦337617 it, and¦337618 he'll¦337619 die¦337619 there¦337618.\x + \xo 12:13: \xt 2Ki 25:7; Jer 52:11.\x*
\v 14 I'll¦337629 also scatter¦337629 all of his assistants¦337624 in every¦337630 direction, and¦337633 I'll¦337634 send out a¦337633 sword¦337633 after¦337635 his entire army.
\v 15 ⇔When¦337642 I scatter¦337642 them¦337643 among¦337644 the nations¦337644 and¦337645 disperse¦337645 them¦337646 throughout the lands¦337647, then¦337637 they'll¦337637 know¦337637 that¦337638 I¦337640 am¦337641 Yahweh¦337641.
\v 16 \add ≈But¦337649\add* I'll¦337649 spare a few of them from¦337653 the¦337653 sword¦337653, famine¦337654, and¦337655 \add ≈deadly diseases\add*, so¦337656 they'll¦337657 be able to record all¦337660 their¦337662 \add ≈hardships and ungodly practices\add* in the \add ≈countries¦337663\add* that I take them to, so¦337668 they'll¦337668 know¦337668 that¦337669 I¦337671 am¦337672 Yahweh¦337672.”
