\v 15 But¦339140 \add Yerushalem,\add* you¦339140 trusted¦339140 in¦339141 your own beauty, and¦339142 you¦339142 acted¦339142 like¦339142 a¦339142 prostitute¦339142 because of¦339145 your¦339145 \add ≈reputation¦339145\add*. You¦339146 \add ≈flirted with everyone¦339154 going past, and prostituted¦339149 yourself\add*, so that your¦339149 beauty became theirs.
\v 16 Then¦339159 you¦339159 took¦339159 your¦339160 clothes¦339160 and¦339161 made¦339161 \add ≈hilltop¦339164 shrines¦339164\add* for yourself with them, decorated in various colours, and¦339166 there you¦339166 acted¦339166 like¦339166 a¦339166 prostitute¦339166. This shouldn't have happened, nor should such a thing exist.
