\v 11 Then¦340154 Yahweh¦340157 \add ≈gave\add* me¦340158 \add another\add* message¦340155:
\v 12 “\add ≈Ask¦340161\add* those rebellious¦340165 \add ≈people\add*, ‘Don't¦340166 you¦340167 know¦340167 what¦340168 those¦340170 \add >things\add* mean? Listen, the¦340175 king¦340175 of¦340175 Bavel¦340177 \add !(Babylon¦340177)\add* came¦340174 to Yerushalem¦340178 \add !(Jerusalem¦340178)\add* and¦340179 captured¦340179 its king and¦340183 its¦340185 princes¦340185 and¦340186 took¦340186 them¦340187 with him¦340188 to¦340189 Bavel¦340189.\x + \xo 17:12-15: \xt 2Ki 24:15-20; 2Ch 36:10.\x*
\v 13 Then¦340191 he¦340191 took¦340191 \add a member\add* of¦340192 the royal¦340193 family¦340192, made¦340194 an agreement¦340196 with¦340195 him—\add ≈forcing him to make various commitments\add*. Then¦340197 he¦340197 took¦340197 away the \add ≈country's¦340203\add* \add former\add* powerful people,
\v 14 so the kingdom¦340207 would remain \add ≈subjected and not¦340209 be able to become powerful again\add*. \add However,\add* by keeping the agreement¦340214, the \add ≈country\add* would \add at least\add* survive.
\v 15 But¦340217 \add @the¦340217 king¦340217 of¦340217 Yerushalem¦340217\add* rebelled¦340217 against him¦340219 by¦340220 sending¦340220 his¦340221 ambassadors¦340221 to Mitsrayim¦340222 \add !(Egypt¦340222)\add* to acquire horses¦340226 and¦340227 an army. Will¦340230 he¦340230 succeed¦340230? Will¦340231 the¦340232 one¦340232 doing¦340232 these¦340233 \add >things\add* escape¦340231? If he¦340234 breaks¦340234 the agreement¦340235, will¦340236 he¦340236 \add ≈survive\add*?
\v 16 This is the master¦340242 Yahweh's¦340243 declaration¦340241: As I \add ≈live¦340238\add*, he'll definitely die in¦340247 the¦340247 land of¦340247 the¦340248 king¦340248 who¦340249 made¦340249 him king, the king whose promises¦340255 he¦340252 despised¦340252, and¦340256 whose agreement¦340260 he¦340257 broke¦340257. He'll die in¦340262 the¦340262 middle¦340262 of¦340262 Bavel¦340264.
\v 17 \add Mitsrayim's\add* Par'oh¦340274 \add !(Pharaoh¦340274)\add* with¦340268 \add &his¦340268\add* mighty army¦340268 and¦340270 huge¦340271 horde¦340270 won't¦340267 help him¦340273 in¦340275 battle¦340275, when¦340276 ramps are constructed and¦340278 siege¦340279 walls are built¦340278 up to¦340280 cut¦340280 off¦340280 many¦340282 lives¦340281,
