\p
\v 21 \add ≈However\add*, their sons¦341560 and¦341557 daughters rebelled¦341557 against¦341559 me¦341559. They¦341564 didn't¦341568 \add ≈keep¦341570 my instructions or follow my regulations¦341561\add*, \add even though\add* anyone who obeys them will live¦341577. They disrespected my rest days, so¦341583 I¦341583 determined to¦341584 pour¦341584 my fury out¦341584 on¦341586 them¦341586 to¦341587 satisfy my¦341588 rage¦341585 against them¦341589 in¦341590 the wilderness¦341590.
\v 22 \add ≈But I didn't¦341599 proceed, for¦341597 the¦341597 sake¦341597 of my¦341598 reputation¦341598\add*, so it wouldn't be¦341600 mocked by the¦341602 nations¦341602 \add ≈who saw me\add* bring¦341605 the \add @Israelis\add* out¦341605 \add of Mitsrayim\add* \add !(Egypt)\add*.
