\v 6 \add ≈Now\add* the master¦344084 Yahweh¦344085 says¦344082 this: The¦344087 city¦344087 of¦344087 blood¦344088 \add ≈won't end well\add*—\add it's like\add* a¦344089 cooking pot¦344089 that¦344090 has rust¦344091 in¦344092 it¦344092, and¦344093 that rust¦344093 won't¦344094 come out¦344095 of it¦344096. Take¦344099 piece¦344097 after piece¦344098 out of¦344098 it¦344099, but don't¦344100 \add ≈be choosy about which¦344090 pieces\add*,
\v 7 because¦344106 \add ≈the blood¦344107 the¦344108 city shed\add* is \add all the way\add* \add ≈through\add* its¦344108 centre. It¦344109 \add ≈displayed the blood\add* on¦344110 a flat rock¦344113 \add to be easily seen\add*, rather than pouring¦344116 it¦344116 out¦344116 on¦344117 the¦344119 ground¦344119 where it¦344121 could be covered¦344120 over with dust¦344122,
\v 8 \add ≈so it makes me angry¦344125 enough to¦344126\add* get revenge: I¦344128 placed¦344128 \em the city's\em* blood¦344131 on¦344132 the smooth rock¦344135, so it couldn't be¦344137 covered¦344137.
\p
\v 9 Therefore, the master¦344143 Yahweh¦344144 says¦344142 this: The¦344146 city¦344146 of¦344146 blood¦344147 \add ≈won't end well\add*. I'll¦344151 also¦344148 enlarge the¦344152 pile¦344152 of \add fire\add*wood¦344152 \add to put underneath it\add*.
\v 10 \add ≈Stack up\add* the¦344155 wood¦344155 and kindle¦344156 the¦344157 fire¦344157. \add ≈Cook the¦344159 meat¦344159 well\add* and¦344160 mix¦344160 in the¦344161 spices¦344161 and¦344162 let¦344163 the¦344162 bones¦344162 be¦344163 charred¦344163.
\v 11 Then¦344165 put¦344165 the empty¦344169 pot onto \add the hot\add* coals¦344168 in order to heat and scorch its¦344175 bronze¦344173, so¦344174 the impurities in it¦344174 will¦344174 be¦344174 melted¦344174—its¦344176 corrosion \add ≈eaten¦344177 away\add*.’
\v 12 \add ?≈That was a lot of work¦344180, but¦344182\add* the¦344186 fire¦344188 didn't¦344182 remove the corrosion from¦344185 it¦344185.
\v 13 Your shameful behaviour is in¦344191 your uncleanness. Because¦344193 you wouldn't \add ≈accept it when¦344195\add* I¦344194 tried to cleanse¦344194 you¦344194, you¦344196 won't¦344198 be¦344199 purified anymore until¦344202 I've¦344204 satisfied my¦344207 fury¦344207 against you¦344208.
\v 14 I¦344210, Yahweh¦344211, have¦344212 declared it¦344213, and¦344214 I¦344214 will¦344214 do¦344214 it. I¦344217 won't¦344218 relent, nor will¦344220 I¦344222 rest from it. \add ≈You'll be judged¦344225 by your¦344223 own practices¦344224 and¦344224 your¦344224 own behaviour¦344223\add*. That's the¦344226 master¦344227 Yahweh's¦344228 declaration.”
