\v 20 “Yahweh¦344313 \add ≈gave me\add* a message¦344311,” I¦344309 answered¦344309 them¦344310,
\v 21 “to¦344320 tell the¦344320 \add ≈Israeli¦344321 people\add* that the master¦344325 Yahweh¦344326 says¦344324 this to¦344328 them: Listen, I'll desecrate¦344328 my¦344331 sanctuary¦344331—the¦344332 pride¦344332 of¦344332 your¦344333 power¦344333, the¦344334 delight of¦344334 your¦344335 eyes¦344335, and¦344336 the¦344336 yearning of your¦344337 soul—and¦344338 \add also\add* your¦344338 sons¦344338 and¦344339 daughters¦344339 who¦344340 you¦344341 left¦344341 behind \add there in Yerushalem\add* \add !(Jerusalem)\add* will be killed by¦344342 the sword¦344342.
\v 22 \add ≈When¦344345 that happens,\add* you¦344345 \add people\add* will¦344345 do¦344345 exactly as¦344346 I've¦344347 done¦344347: you¦344352 won't¦344355 veil your beards, or eat¦344356 the bread¦344353 of¦344353 mourning men¦344354,
\v 23 \add ≈but¦344358 instead\add* your¦344358 turbans¦344358 will¦344359 be¦344359 on¦344359 your¦344361 heads¦344361, and¦344362 your¦344362 sandals¦344362 on¦344363 your¦344363 feet¦344363. You¦344365 won't¦344366 mourn or weep¦344367, because you'll¦344368 melt away¦344368 \add ≈due to your¦344369 disobedience\add*, and¦344370 everyone will¦344370 groan¦344370 for \add ≈their relatives¦344374\add*.
\v 24 \add ≈So¦344376\add* Yehezkel¦344377 \add !(Ezekiel¦344377)\add* will be a¦344379 sign¦344379 for you, because¦344387 when¦344385 that time comes¦344385, you'll¦344384 do \add ≈exactly the same as he's¦344383 doing\add*. Then¦344386 you¦344386 \add people\add* will¦344386 know¦344386 that¦344387 I¦344388 am the master¦344389 Yahweh¦344390.’ ”
\p
\v 25 “But¦344393 you¦344393, son¦344394 of¦344394 humanity¦344396, on¦344398 the day¦344398 that I capture their temple, (which is their joy¦344404, their¦344405 pride, and what they see and desire¦344408), and¦344410 when I take¦344399 away their¦344413 sons¦344414 and¦344415 daughters¦344415,
\v 26 a refugee will¦344419 come¦344419 to you here on that¦344418 day¦344417 to¦344421 give you¦344421 the news¦344422.
\v 27 At that¦344426 time¦344425, your¦344428 mouth¦344428 will¦344427 be¦344427 opened¦344427 up to that refugee and¦344432 you'll¦344432 speak¦344432 \add again\add*—you'll¦344434 no longer be¦344434 silent¦344434. You'll¦344436 be a¦344438 sign¦344438 for them so¦344439 that they'll¦344439 know¦344439 that¦344440 I¦344442 am¦344443 Yahweh¦344443.”
