\v 1 \add ≈At the¦346026 beginning of January\add* in the twelfth year¦346025 \add since King Yehoyakin had been taken captive\add*, Yahweh¦346034 \add ≈gave me¦346035\add* a message¦346032:
\v 2 “Son¦346038 of¦346038 humanity¦346040, \add ≈stand firmly\add* against Mitsrayim's¦346047 \add !(Egypt¦346047)\add* king¦346046 Par'oh¦346045 \add !(Pharaoh¦346045)\add*.\x + \xo 29:2: \xt Isa 19:1-25; Jer 46:2-26.\x* Prophesy¦346048 against him¦346049 and¦346050 against all¦346053 of Mitsrayim¦346052,
\v 3 telling \add them\add* that the master¦346061 Yahweh¦346062 says this: Listen, I'm¦346063 against you¦346064, Par'oh¦346065, king¦346066 of¦346066 Mitsrayim¦346068—you, the¦346069 great¦346070 sea¦346069 monster¦346069 that¦346071 lurks in¦346072 the¦346072 middle¦346072 of¦346073 the river, who says¦346075, “My river¦346077 is my¦346077 own. I've made¦346079 it for¦346079 myself¦346079.”
\v 4 I'll¦346081 put¦346081 hooks¦346082 into¦346084 your¦346084 \add #jaw¦346084\add*, and¦346085 the¦346086 fish¦346086 from your¦346088 streams will cling to¦346089 the scales¦346089 on your¦346089 \add side\add*. I'll¦346090 lift you¦346090 up¦346090 from¦346091 the middle of your¦346092 river, along with all¦346094 the¦346096 river's fish¦346096 that cling to your scales.
\v 5 I'll¦346101 fling you¦346101 into¦346102 the¦346102 wilderness¦346102—you¦346103 and¦346104 all¦346105 the¦346107 fish¦346107 from your¦346108 river. You'll¦346115 fall¦346113 on¦346109 the open countryside¦346112—\add @your¦346113 corpse¦346113\add* won't¦346114 be taken or moved, \add but rather\add* I'll¦346122 give¦346122 you¦346117 as food¦346123 to¦346118 the \add #birds¦346120\add* and wild animals¦346118.
\v 6 Then¦346125 all¦346126 of¦346126 Mitsrayim's¦346129 inhabitants¦346128 will¦346125 know¦346125 that¦346130 I¦346131 am¦346132 Yahweh¦346132, because¦346133 they've¦346134 been¦346134 \add like a brittle\add* reed¦346136 to the¦346137 \add ≈kingdom\add* of¦346137 Yisrael¦346138 \add !(Israel¦346138)\add*.\x + \xo 29:6: \xt Isa 36:6.\x*
\v 7 When¦346140 \add @Yisrael¦346141\add* \add ≈grabbed¦346140 you¦346144\add*, you¦346145 broke¦346145 and tore open their shoulder¦346149, and¦346150 when¦346150 they leaned¦346150 on¦346151 you¦346151, you¦346152 broke¦346152 and¦346153 made¦346153 their legs unsteady.
\v 8 Therefore the master¦346163 Yahweh¦346164 says¦346162 this: Listen, I'll¦346165 send¦346166 \add ≈an army\add* against you¦346167 that will¦346169 cut¦346169 short both people's and¦346172 animals'¦346172 \add lives\add*,
\v 9 and¦346174 Mitsrayim¦346177 will¦346174 become¦346174 a¦346178 \add ≈desolate¦346178\add* ruin¦346179. Then¦346180 they'll¦346180 know¦346180 that¦346181 I¦346183 am¦346184 Yahweh¦346184.
\p Because¦346185 the sea monster said¦346186, “The¦346187 river¦346187 is mine, because I made¦346190 it,”
\v 10 listen: I'm¦346193 against¦346194 you¦346194 and¦346195 against your¦346197 river, so¦346198 I'll¦346198 give Mitsrayim¦346202 over to¦346203 desolation¦346205 and waste, and you'll become a¦346205 wasteland¦346205 from¦346206 the Migdol¦346206 to Seveneh¦346207 and¦346208 the¦346210 \add #borders¦346210\add* of¦346210 Kush¦346211 \add !(Ethiopia¦346211)\add*.
\v 11 No person or domestic animal¦346220 will¦346222 pass¦346222 through it¦346224, and¦346225 it¦346226 won't be inhabited for forty¦346227 years¦346228.
\v 12 I'll¦346230 make¦346230 Mitsrayim¦346234 a¦346235 desolation¦346235 in¦346236 the¦346236 middle¦346236 of uninhabited¦346239 lands¦346238, and¦346240 its¦346240 cities will become a desolation in¦346241 the¦346241 middle¦346241 of wasted¦346243 cities for forty¦346246 years¦346247, then¦346248 I'll¦346248 scatter¦346248 \add ≈the Mitsri¦346251\add* \add !(Egyptian¦346251)\add* \add ≈people\add* among¦346252 the nations¦346252, and¦346253 I'll¦346253 disperse¦346253 them¦346253 through the lands¦346254.
\p
\v 13 \add ≈But\add* the master¦346260 Yahweh¦346261 says¦346259 this: At the¦346262 end¦346262 of forty¦346263 years¦346264 I'll¦346265 gather¦346265 Mitsrayim¦346268 from¦346269 the¦346271 people¦346271 groups they¦346274 were¦346274 scattered¦346274 among,
\v 14 and¦346277 I'll¦346277 restore Mitsrayim's¦346281 fortunes and¦346282 bring¦346282 them¦346283 back to the¦346284 region¦346284 of¦346284 Patros¦346285, to¦346286 their¦346289 native land. Then¦346290 they'll¦346290 become an insignificant¦346293 kingdom¦346292 there¦346291.
\v 15 It'll¦346298 be the¦346297 least significant kingdom¦346297, and¦346300 it¦346302 won't \add ≈become prominent\add* again¦346303 among the¦346306 nations¦346306. I'll¦346307 diminish them¦346307 so that they'll no longer \add ≈dominate¦346309\add* \add other\add* nations¦346310.
\v 16 \add Requesting help from\add* \add @Mitsrayim¦346313\add* will¦346313 no longer be a reason for¦346316 the¦346316 \add ≈kingdom\add* of¦346316 Yisrael¦346317 \add !(Israel¦346317)\add* to¦346318 \add ≈be confident¦346318\add*, instead, \add @Mitsrayim\add* will be a¦346318 reminder¦346319 of Yisrael's \add ≈disobedience\add* when¦346321 they turned¦346321 to \add @Mitsrayim\add* for help. Then¦346323 they'll¦346323 know¦346323 that¦346324 I¦346325 am the master¦346326 Yahweh¦346327.”
\s1 Nevukadnetsar's defeat of Mitsrayim
\rem /s1 King Nebuchadnezzar Will Conquer Egypt; Nebuchadnezzar to Conquer Egypt; Babylonia Will Plunder Egypt
\p
\v 17 \add ≈At the beginning of May\add* in¦346331 the 27th year¦346333 \add since King Yehoyakin had been taken captive\add*,\f + \fr 29:17 \ft 571 B.C.\f* Yahweh¦346340 \add ≈gave me¦346341\add* a message¦346338:
\v 18 “Son¦346344 of¦346344 humanity¦346346, the¦346348 Babylonian King¦346348 Nevukadnetsar¦346347 \add !(Nebuchadnezzar¦346347)\add* stationed his army to do hard work against¦346357 \add the fortified island city of\add* Tsor¦346359 \add !(Tyre¦346359)\add*. Every¦346360 head¦346362 was rubbed until it was made¦346363 bald¦346363, and¦346364 every¦346364 shoulder¦346366 was¦346367 made¦346367 raw. Yet he and his army received no payment from¦346374 Tsor¦346374 for the¦346377 hard work¦346377 that¦346378 he¦346380 carried out against it¦346381,
\v 19 therefore the master¦346387 Yahweh¦346388 says¦346386 this, ‘Listen, I'm¦346389 giving¦346390 Mitsrayim¦346398 \add !(Egypt¦346398)\add* to¦346391 the¦346392 Babylonian King¦346392 Nevukadnetsar¦346391 and¦346399 he'll¦346399 take¦346399 away its¦346400 wealth¦346400, plunder its¦346402 possessions, and¦346403 carry¦346399 off¦346399 everything he¦346403 finds there—that will be¦346405 his¦346407 army's¦346407 wages¦346406.
\v 20 I've¦346414 given¦346414 him¦346415 the¦346418 land¦346418 of¦346418 Mitsrayim¦346419 as the wages¦346409 for¦346413 the work they¦346421 did¦346421 for me¦346422. That's¦346420 the¦346423 master¦346424 Yahweh's¦346425 declaration¦346423.
\p
\v 21 On that day¦346428 I'll¦346430 make¦346430 \add ≈power\add* sprout up for¦346432 the¦346432 \add ≈kingdom\add* of¦346432 Yisrael¦346433 \add !(Israel¦346433)\add*, and¦346434 I'll¦346435 \add ≈put you¦346434 among¦346439 them¦346439 to speak¦346438 out\add* so¦346440 they'll¦346440 know¦346440 that¦346441 I¦346443 am¦346444 Yahweh¦346444.’ ”
\c 30
\s1 Yahweh's punishment of Mitsrayim
\rem /s1 A Lament for Egypt; Lamentation for Egypt; The Lord Will Punish Egypt; A Sad Day for Egypt
\p
\v 1 Then¦346447 Yahweh¦346450 \add ≈gave\add* me¦346451 \add another\add* message¦346448:
\q1
\v 2 “Son¦346454 of¦346454 humanity¦346456, prophesy¦346457 and¦346458 say¦346458 that the master¦346461 Yahweh¦346462 says¦346460 this:
\q1 ‘Wail¦346463 \add now\add* \add ≈because¦346465 the coming days¦346465 won't go well\add*.
\q1
\v 3 The day is¦346469 near¦346469—the day¦346470 is¦346471 near¦346471 for¦346473 Yahweh¦346473.
\q1 It'll¦346478 be a¦346474 day¦346474 of¦346474 clouds¦346475—a¦346476 time¦346476 of¦346476 doom for nations¦346477.
\q1
\v 4 Then¦346480 \add ≈an army\add* will¦346480 come¦346480 against Mitsrayim¦346482 \add !(Egypt¦346482)\add*,
\q1 and¦346483 there'll be¦346483 anguish¦346484 in Kush¦346485 \add !(Ethiopia¦346485)\add* when¦346486 the¦346487 people¦346489 are killed¦346487 in¦346488 Mitsrayim¦346488—
\q1 when¦346489 they take¦346489 its wealth¦346490,
\q1 and when its¦346490 foundations¦346492 get torn¦346491 apart.
\p
\v 5 Kush¦346494 and¦346495 Put¦346495, Ludia, all¦346497 Arav, and¦346500 Libya¦346500, together with the people belonging to the agreement¦346503—they'll¦346506 all be killed by¦346505 the sword¦346505.
\v 6 Yahweh¦346511 says¦346510 this: The ones who¦346513 support¦346513 Mitsrayim¦346514 \add militarily\add* will¦346512 fall¦346512, and¦346515 the¦346516 pride¦346516 of¦346516 \add @Mitsrayim's¦346517\add* strength¦346517 will \add ≈collapse\add*. From¦346518 Migdol¦346518 to Seveneh¦346519 \add @their combined warriors\add* will be killed by¦346520 the sword¦346520. That's the master¦346525 Yahweh's¦346526 declaration¦346524.
\v 7 \add @Those¦346528 allies¦346528\add* will¦346528 be¦346528 appalled there among the¦346529 abandoned lands¦346530, and¦346532 their cities will be among all the \add other\add* ruined cities.
\v 8 Then¦346539 they'll¦346539 know¦346539 that¦346540 I¦346542 am¦346543 Yahweh¦346543, when¦346544 I¦346544 set¦346544 fire¦346546 to Mitsrayim¦346547, and¦346548 when all¦346549 its¦346551 helpers¦346551 are¦346548 destroyed¦346548.
\p
\v 9 \add ≈At that¦346554 time\add*, messengers¦346556 will¦346555 go¦346555 out¦346555 from¦346557 \add ≈in¦346557 front¦346557 of¦346557\add* me¦346557 in¦346558 ships¦346558 to¦346559 terrorise Kush¦346562 \add ≈when they think they're secure¦346563\add*, and¦346564 there'll be anguish¦346565 among¦346566 them¦346566 on¦346567 the day¦346567 of¦346568 Mitsrayim's¦346568 doom. \add ≈Yes, take notice,\add* it's¦346571 coming¦346571.
\v 10 The master¦346576 Yahweh¦346577 says¦346575 this: I'll¦346578 \add ≈use\add* the Babylonian King¦346585 Nevukadnetsar¦346584 \add !(Nebuchadnezzar¦346584)\add* to bring Mitsrayim's¦346582 \add #multitudes¦346581\add* to an¦346578 end¦346578.
\v 11 He¦346589 and¦346590 his¦346590 army with¦346591 him¦346591, the terror of¦346592 nations¦346593, will¦346594 be¦346594 brought¦346594 in to¦346595 destroy¦346595 the¦346596 land¦346596. They'll¦346597 draw¦346597 out their¦346598 swords¦346598 against Mitsrayim¦346601 and¦346602 fill¦346602 the¦346605 land¦346605 with those they kill.
\v 12 I'll¦346608 make¦346608 the rivers into dry¦346610 ground¦346610, and¦346611 I'll¦346611 sell¦346611 the¦346614 land¦346614 into¦346615 the¦346615 hands¦346615 of¦346615 wicked¦346617 \add >men\add*. I'll¦346618 make the¦346619 land¦346619 and¦346620 its abundant \add produce\add* desolate¦346618 by¦346621 the¦346621 actions of¦346621 strangers¦346623. I¦346624, Yahweh¦346625, have¦346626 spoken¦346626.
\p
\v 13 The master¦346632 Yahweh¦346633 says¦346631 this: I'll¦346634 destroy¦346634 idols¦346635, and¦346636 I'll¦346636 bring an end¦346636 to¦346636 the worthless¦346637 idols¦346637 in Nof¦346638 \add !(Memphis¦346638)\add*. There won't¦346643 be a¦346639 prince¦346639 in the¦346640 land¦346640 of¦346640 Mitsrayim¦346642 any longer, and¦346647 I'll¦346647 put¦346647 terror into¦346649 Mitsrayim¦346650.
\v 14 Then¦346652 I'll¦346652 make \add the\add* Patros¦346655 \add region\add* desolate¦346652 and¦346656 set¦346656 fire¦346657 to Tsoan¦346658 \add city\add*, and¦346659 I'll¦346659 execute \add #judgement¦346660\add* against No¦346661 \add !(Thebes¦346661)\add* \add (the capital of southern Mitsrayim)\add*.
\v 15 I'll¦346663 pour¦346663 out¦346663 my¦346664 fury¦346664 on¦346665 Mitsrayim's¦346669 stronghold¦346668 Sin¦346667, and¦346670 cut¦346670 off¦346670 the¦346673 crowd¦346673 at No¦346674.
\v 16 Then¦346676 I'll¦346676 set¦346676 fire¦346677 to Mitsrayim¦346678: Sin will be in¦346679 great agony¦346679, No¦346683 will be¦346685 broken¦346685 up, and¦346686 Nof¦346686 will face enemies¦346687 every day¦346688.
\v 17 The¦346690 young¦346690 men¦346690 of¦346690 Aven and¦346692 Pi¦346692-Beset \add cities\add* will be killed by¦346695 the sword¦346695, and their \add ≈populations will be taken\add* into¦346698 captivity¦346698.
\v 18 In¦346701 \add Mitsrayim's\add* Tahfanhes¦346701, the¦346703 day¦346703 will¦346702 hold back its light when¦346704 I break¦346704 Mitsrayim's¦346710 \add ≈power and control\add* there¦346706, and¦346711 its pride¦346714 in its¦346715 strength¦346715 will be finished. There'll be a¦346717 cloud¦346717 covering¦346718 it¦346718, and¦346719 its¦346719 daughters¦346719 will \add ≈be taken away\add* into¦346720 captivity¦346720.
\v 19 I'll¦346723 execute acts of judgement¦346724 in Mitsrayim¦346725, then¦346726 they'll¦346726 know¦346726 that¦346727 I¦346729 am¦346730 Yahweh¦346730.’ ”
\s1 Yahweh breaks Mitsrayim's power
\rem /s1 The Broken Arms of Pharaoh; The Broken Power of the King of Egypt; Proclamation against Pharaoh
\p
\v 20 \add ≈At the beginning of May\add* in¦346734 the eleventh year¦346736 \add since King Yehoyakin had been taken captive\add*,\f + \fr 30:20 \ft (Back in time to) 587 B.C.\f* Yahweh¦346743 \add ≈gave me¦346744\add* a message¦346741:
\v 21 “Son¦346747 of¦346747 humanity¦346749, I've¦346757 broken¦346757 the Mitsri¦346756 \add !(Egyptian¦346756)\add* king¦346754 Par'oh's¦346753 \add !(Pharaoh¦346753)\add* arm¦346752. Listen¦346758, it¦346761 hasn't been¦346761 \add ≈put¦346764 in a¦346765 splint\add*, or set to¦346766 heal with a bandage¦346766, so¦346758 that it'll become strong¦346767 enough \add again\add* to¦346768 hold a sword¦346769.
\v 22 Therefore the master¦346777 Yahweh¦346778 says¦346775 this, ‘Listen, I'm¦346779 against¦346780 the¦346783 Mitsri¦346785 king¦346783 Par'oh¦346782 and¦346786 I'll¦346786 break¦346786 both his¦346789 strong¦346792 arm¦346792 and¦346793 the¦346795 \add previously\add* broken¦346795 one, and¦346796 I'll¦346796 make¦346796 the¦346799 sword¦346799 fall¦346796 from¦346800 his¦346800 \add ≈grip\add*.
\v 23 Then¦346802 I'll¦346802 scatter¦346802 Mitsrayim¦346805 \add !(Egypt¦346805)\add* among¦346806 the \add other\add* nations¦346806 and¦346807 disperse¦346807 \add @their¦346807 people¦346807\add* among¦346808 the lands¦346808.
\v 24 I'll¦346810 strengthen¦346810 the Babylonian king's arms and¦346816 place¦346816 my¦346819 sword¦346819 in¦346820 his¦346820 hand¦346820 so¦346821 that I¦346821 can destroy¦346821 Par'oh's¦346825 arms¦346824. He'll¦346826 groan¦346826 \add ≈in¦346829 front¦346829 of¦346829\add* the Babylonian king with the¦346827 groans¦346827 of¦346827 a dying man.
\v 25 I'll¦346831 strengthen¦346831 the¦346834 arms¦346834 of¦346834 the¦346835 Babylonian king¦346835, while Par'oh's¦346838 arms¦346837 will¦346839 fall¦346839. Then¦346840 they'll¦346840 know¦346840 that¦346841 I¦346843 am¦346844 Yahweh¦346844, when¦346845 I put¦346845 my¦346846 sword¦346846 into¦346847 the¦346847 hand¦346847 of¦346847 the¦346848 king¦346848 of¦346848 Bavel¦346850 \add !(Babylon¦346850)\add* and¦346851 he¦346851 \add ≈uses\add* it¦346852 against¦346853 Mitsrayim¦346856.
\v 26 I'll¦346858 scatter¦346858 Mitsrayim¦346861 among¦346862 the \add other\add* nations¦346862 and¦346863 disperse¦346863 \add @their¦346864 people¦346864\add* through the lands¦346865. Then¦346866 they'll¦346866 know¦346866 that¦346867 I¦346869 am¦346870 Yahweh¦346870.”
\c 31
\s1 Mitsrayim gets compared to fallen Ashur
\rem /s1 Egypt Is Compared to a Cedar Tree; A Cedar in Lebanon; Egypt Compared to Fallen Assyria; The Lofty Cedar
\p
\v 1 \add ≈At the end of June\add* in¦346874 the eleventh year¦346876 \add since King Yehoyakin had been taken captive\add*,\f + \fr 31:1 \ft 587 B.C.\f* Yahweh¦346883 \add ≈gave me¦346884\add* a message¦346881:
\v 2 “Son¦346887 of¦346887 humanity¦346889, \add ≈ask¦346890\add* the¦346894 Mitsri¦346896 \add !(Egyptian¦346896)\add* king¦346894 Par'oh¦346893 \add !(Pharaoh¦346893)\add* and¦346897 his¦346899 \add #multitudes¦346899\add* around him, ‘\add ≈Who¦346902 else is¦346903 as powerful as you¦346903 and your¦346904 people\add*?
\v 3 Listen, Ashur¦346907 \add !(Assyria¦346907)\add* was¦346908 \add like\add* a¦346908 cedar¦346908 in¦346909 Levanon¦346909 with beautiful¦346910 branches¦346911, giving¦346913 shade¦346913 to the forest¦346912—extremely tall¦346914, and¦346916 the branches¦346917 formed its¦346919 treetop¦346919.
\v 4 \add ≈A deep¦346923 water¦346921 supply\add* made¦346922 it¦346922 grow¦346922 tall. Rivers¦346927 flowed all around¦346929 its¦346930 area, because their channels¦346933 stretched out¦346934 to¦346935 all¦346936 the¦346938 trees¦346938 in the¦346939 countryside¦346939.
\v 5 It¦346944 \add ≈grew taller¦346944\add* than¦346946 any of the¦346947 other trees¦346947 in the¦346948 countryside¦346948, and¦346949 its¦346950 branches¦346952 grew long¦346951 and \add ≈thick\add* because of \add ≈having plenty¦346955 of\add* \add #water¦346954\add* in its¦346952 shoots.
\v 6 Every¦346960 \add ≈kind of¦346960\add* bird¦346962 nested¦346959 in its¦346965 branches¦346965, while every¦346967 living thing in the¦346969 countryside¦346969 gave¦346966 birth¦346966 to its young under the¦346968 foliage of¦346968 that tree. All¦346972 the powerful¦346974 nations¦346973 lived under its¦346970 shade¦346970.
\v 7 It¦346976 was¦346976 beautiful¦346976 in¦346977 its¦346977 greatness¦346977 and due to the¦346978 length¦346978 of¦346978 its¦346979 branches¦346979, because¦346980 its¦346983 \add #roots¦346983\add* \add ≈had access to¦346984\add* many¦346987 water¦346986 \add sources\add*.
\v 8 Cedar¦346989 trees in¦346993 God's garden¦346993\x + \xo 31:8: \xt Gen 2:9.\x* couldn't equal it. None of¦346993 the cypress trees¦346996 matched its branches, nor could its branches be equalled by the plane¦347002 tree¦347002. There was¦347005 no other tree¦347009 in¦347010 God's garden that could compare to¦347016 its¦347017 beauty¦347017.
\v 9 I¦347020 made¦347020 it¦347020 beautiful¦347019 with its¦347022 many branches¦347022, and¦347023 all¦347024 the¦347026 trees¦347026 in¦347030 God's garden¦347030 in Eden¦347028 envied¦347023 it¦347023.
\p
\v 10 Therefore the master¦347037 Yahweh¦347038 says¦347036 this: Because¦347039 it was¦347041 so¦347034 tall¦347041, and¦347043 it¦347043 set its¦347044 treetop¦347044 between¦347047 its branches¦347048, and¦347049 \add ≡because¦347039\add* it¦347049 \add ≈grew proud\add* of¦347050 its¦347050 height¦347051,
\v 11 I¦347053 \add ≈handed¦347054 it¦347053 over to\add* a¦347055 powerful nation¦347056 to¦347059 deal with it¦347059 according¦347060 to¦347060 what its¦347060 wickedness¦347060 deserves. I've¦347061 thrown it¦347061 out¦347061,
\v 12 and¦347063 foreigners¦347064 who were the terror of¦347065 all the nations¦347066 cut¦347063 it¦347063 off and¦347067 left¦347067 it¦347067 to¦347068 die. Its branches fell¦347074 onto the¦347070 mountains¦347070 and¦347071 all¦347071 the¦347073 valleys¦347073, and¦347076 lay broken¦347076 in¦347078 all¦347078 the¦347079 land's ravines¦347079. Then all the¦347080 nations on earth¦347080 came¦347081 out from¦347082 under its¦347082 shade¦347082 and¦347087 went¦347081 away from it¦347087.
\v 13 All¦347093 the \add ≈various kinds of¦347093\add* \add #birds¦347095\add* rested on the¦347095 trunk¦347091 of¦347095 the¦347096 fallen¦347091 tree, and¦347097 every¦347101 \add kind of\add* animal¦347102 in the¦347103 countryside¦347103 came to its¦347099 branches¦347099.
\v 14 That happened so¦347105 that¦347105 no other trees that¦347106 grow by the waters will raise¦347109 up¦347109 their¦347137 foliage to the height of the tallest trees¦347113, and¦347116 that no other trees that grow beside the waters will reach up to¦347122 that height¦347130. They've¦347138 all¦347137 been¦347138 assigned to¦347139 death¦347139, to¦347140 the¦347142 earth¦347142 below, among humanity's¦347146 children¦347145, with those¦347149 that¦347149 go¦347149 down¦347149 into the¦347150 pit¦347150.
\p
\v 15 The master¦347156 Yahweh¦347157 says¦347155 this: On¦347158 the day¦347158 when the cedar went¦347159 down¦347159 to¦347160 \add ≈the place of the dead\add*, I¦347161 brought mourning¦347161 to the earth. I¦347162 covered¦347162 the¦347166 deep¦347166 waters over it, and¦347167 I held back the oceans. I held back the great waters¦347170, and¦347172 I¦347172 brought mourning¦347172 to Levanon¦347174 for it. So¦347175 all¦347175 the¦347177 trees¦347177 in the¦347178 countryside¦347178 mourned because of it¦347179.
\v 16 I¦347184 brought¦347186 shuddering to the nations¦347185 at the¦347182 sound¦347182 of¦347182 its¦347183 downfall¦347183, when¦347186 I¦347186 threw it¦347187 down to¦347188 \add ≈the place of the dead\add*, along with¦347189 those¦347191 who¦347191 went¦347191 down¦347191 into the¦347192 pit¦347192. So¦347193 I comforted¦347193 all¦347196 the¦347198 trees¦347198 from Eden¦347200 in the lowest¦347195 parts of the earth¦347194. Those had been the¦347201 choicest¦347201 and¦347202 best trees from Levanon¦347204—the trees that drank the \add #waters¦347208\add*.
\v 17 They also¦347210 went¦347214 down¦347214 with \add @the big tree\add* to¦347215 \add ≈the place of the dead\add*, to¦347216 the ones who'd been killed¦347218 by the sword¦347220. Those were its strong arm¦347221—those nations¦347225 who'd lived¦347222 in¦347223 its¦347223 shade¦347223.
\p
\v 18 \add Mitsrayim\add* \add !(Egypt)\add*, which of the trees in Eden was¦347230 your equal in¦347232 glory¦347232 and¦347233 greatness¦347233? You'll¦347237 be¦347237 brought¦347237 down¦347237 with¦347239 Eden's¦347243 trees to¦347244 the lowest¦347247 parts of the¦347246 earth¦347246 among¦347234 the¦347234 uncircumcised¦347249. You'll¦347250 live there with¦347251 those¦347253 who were killed¦347253 by the sword¦347255.’
\m That's¦347256 \add the fate of\add* Par'oh¦347257 \add !(Pharaoh¦347257)\add* and¦347258 all¦347258 his¦347260 \add #multitudes¦347260\add*. That's the¦347262 master¦347263 Yahweh's¦347264 declaration¦347262.”
\c 32
\s1 Mourning over Mitsrayim and its king
\rem /s1 A Lament for Pharaoh; A Warning for Pharaoh; The King of Egypt Is Compared to a Crocodile; Lamentation over Pharaoh and Egypt
\p
\v 1 \add ≈At the beginning of¦347268 March\add* in¦347271 the twelfth year¦347270 \add since King Yehoyakin had been taken captive\add*,\f + \fr 32:1 \ft 585 B.C.\f* Yahweh¦347280 \add ≈gave me¦347281\add* a message¦347278:
\v 2 “Son¦347284 of¦347284 humanity¦347286, \add ≈sing a¦347288 loud mourning¦347288 song\add* about the¦347292 Mitsri¦347294 \add !(Egyptian¦347294)\add* King¦347292 Par'oh¦347291 \add !(Pharaoh¦347291)\add* and¦347295 tell¦347295 him¦347296,
\q1 ‘You're like a¦347297 young¦347297 lion¦347297 among the nations¦347298,
\q1 but¦347300 you're¦347300 like¦347301 the¦347301 sea¦347302 monster¦347301 in¦347302 the¦347302 oceans¦347302—
\q1 you¦347303 churn up the water—
\q1 you stir up the waters¦347307 with¦347308 your¦347308 feet¦347308, making¦347305 them muddy.
\q1
\v 3 The master¦347314 Yahweh¦347315 says¦347313 this:
\q1 I'll¦347316 spread¦347316 my net over¦347317 you¦347317 in the assembly of many¦347323 people¦347322 groups,
\q1 and¦347324 they'll¦347324 haul you¦347324 up¦347324 in¦347325 my net.
\q1
\v 4 I'll¦347327 abandon¦347327 you¦347327 in¦347328 the¦347328 land¦347328.
\q1 I'll¦347333 throw¦347333 you¦347333 into the countryside¦347332
\q1 and¦347334 cause¦347334 \add ≈every¦347336 kind of¦347336\add* bird¦347338 to¦347334 settle¦347334 on¦347335 you¦347335,
\q1 and¦347340 animals¦347342 of¦347342 \add ≈every¦347343 kind of¦347343\add* will gorge¦347340 themselves on you¦347341.
\q1
\v 5 I'll¦347347 \add ≈dump\add* your¦347350 flesh¦347350 on¦347351 the¦347353 hills¦347353,
\q1 and¦347354 fill¦347354 the¦347355 valleys¦347355 with your¦347356 corpse.
