\q1 nor will cattle hooves¦347480 disturb them¦347483.
\q1
\v 14 Then¦347485 I'll¦347486 calm their¦347487 waters¦347487 and¦347488 make their¦347488 rivers¦347488 run like¦347489 oil¦347489.
\q1 That's the¦347491 master¦347492 Yahweh's¦347493 declaration¦347491.
\p
\v 15 When¦347495 I make¦347495 Mitsrayim's¦347499 territory into an abandoned place,
\q1 when¦347501 the¦347502 land¦347502 is \add ≈stripped of¦347503 all its¦347503 produce\add*,
\q1 when¦347504 I¦347504 attack¦347504 all¦347507 its inhabitants¦347509, they'll¦347511 know¦347511 that¦347512 I¦347514 am¦347515 Yahweh¦347515.
\q1
\v 16 There'll be¦347517 a \add ≈funeral song\add*—the¦347520 daughters¦347520 of¦347520 the¦347521 nations¦347521 will¦347522 sing mournful songs about it¦347523.
\q1 They'll sing sadly about Mitsrayim¦347526—over all¦347529 its¦347531 \add #multitudes¦347531\add* they'll¦347532 sing dirges.
\q1 That's the¦347534 master¦347535 Yahweh's¦347536 declaration¦347534.’ ”
\s1 Those in the place of the dead
\rem /s1 The World of the Dead; Egypt Falls into the Pit; Dirge over Egypt
\p
\v 17 \add ≈In¦347540 the middle of that same month¦347545\add*,\f + \fr 32:17 \ft 585 B.C.\f* Yahweh¦347549 \add ≈gave me¦347550\add* a message¦347547:
\v 18 “Son¦347553 of¦347553 humanity¦347555, weep for the¦347559 \add ≈numerous Mitsrim\add* \add !(Egyptians)\add* and¦347561 bring¦347561 them down¦347561 to¦347566 the¦347569 lowest¦347569 parts¦347569 of the¦347568 earth¦347568. \add ≡Bring¦347561\add* \add @Mitsrayim¦347562\add* \add !(Egypt¦347562)\add* and¦347563 the¦347563 daughters¦347563 of¦347563 majestic nations¦347564 down along with¦347570 those¦347572 who've \add already\add* gone¦347572 down¦347572 into the¦347573 pit¦347573.
\v 19 \add Ask them: Mitsrayim,\add* are you \add really\add* more¦347575 beautiful than¦347575 anyone else? Go¦347577 down¦347577 and¦347578 lie down with¦347579 the uncircumcised¦347581.
\p
\v 20 They'll¦347587 fall¦347587 among those¦347584 who were killed¦347584 by the sword¦347586. The sword¦347588 has¦347590 been drawn¦347590. \add @Mitsrayim¦347589\add* has¦347589 been¦347589 handed over to the sword—\add @its¦347590 enemies¦347590\add* will seize it¦347591 and¦347592 its¦347594 multitudes¦347594.
\v 21 The¦347599 strongest of¦347599 the¦347600 warriors¦347600 in \add ≈the¦347601 place of¦347601 the dead\add* will declare about¦347605 \add @Mitsrayim¦347605\add* and its allies, ‘They've¦347606 come¦347606 down¦347606 here. They'll¦347607 lie¦347607 with the¦347608 uncircumcised¦347608—with those who were killed¦347609 by the sword¦347611.’
\p
\v 22 Ashur¦347614 \add !(Assyria¦347614)\add* is¦347613 there¦347613 with all¦347615 its¦347617 \add ≈people\add*, with its¦347619 graves¦347619 all around¦347618 it¦347618—all of¦347620 them¦347620 were¦347621 killed¦347621 by¦347623 the sword¦347623.
\v 23 Those whose graves¦347627 are¦347626 set¦347626 in¦347628 the¦347630 pit's¦347630 recesses\x + \xo 32:23 \xt Isa 14:15.\x* are¦347631 there, along with all its¦347632 \add ≈people\add*. Its¦347634 graves surround¦347633 all of¦347635 those¦347635 who were¦347636 killed¦347636 by¦347638 the sword¦347638—those who¦347639 brought terror¦347642 onto the land¦347643 of the¦347644 living¦347644.
\p
\v 24 Eylam is¦347646 there¦347646 with all¦347648 its \add #multitudes¦347650\add*, with its¦347650 \add #graves¦347652\add* all around¦347651 it—all of them¦347653 were¦347654 killed¦347654. \add That's the place for\add* those¦347655 who¦347655 were killed by¦347656 the sword¦347656, who've gone¦347659 down¦347659 uncircumcised¦347660 to¦347662 the¦347665 lowest¦347665 parts¦347665 of the¦347664 earth¦347664, who¦347666 brought their¦347668 \add #terrors¦347668\add* onto the land¦347669 of the¦347670 living¦347670, and¦347671 who carry¦347671 their¦347672 own shame¦347672, together with¦347673 the ones going¦347675 down¦347675 into the¦347676 pit¦347676.
\v 25 They \add ≈prepared¦347680\add* a¦347681 bed¦347681 for¦347682 \add @Eylam¦347682\add* and all¦347683 its¦347685 \add #multitudes¦347685\add* among those who were¦347686 slain—its¦347686 graves¦347687 surround¦347686 it. All of¦347688 them¦347688 are¦347689 uncircumcised¦347689, pierced by the sword¦347692, because¦347693 they brought their¦347696 \add #terrors¦347696\add* onto the land¦347697 of the¦347698 living¦347698. So¦347699 they¦347699 carry¦347699 their¦347700 own shame¦347700, together with¦347701 the ones going down into the pit among all those who've been killed, those who¦347703 are going¦347703 down¦347703 into the¦347704 pit¦347704. \add @Eylam\add* is among all those who were killed.
\p
\v 26 Meshek¦347710, Tuval¦347711, and¦347712 all¦347712 their \add #multitudes¦347714\add* are¦347715 there¦347709 with their graves¦347716 all around¦347715 them. All of them are¦347718 uncircumcised¦347718, killed by the sword¦347720, because¦347721 they¦347723 brought their¦347724 \add #terrors¦347724\add* onto the land¦347725 of the¦347726 living¦347726.
\v 27 They¦347729 don't¦347728 lie¦347729 with¦347730 the fallen¦347733 warriors of the uncircumcised¦347734 who've gone¦347736 down¦347736 to \add ≈the place of the dead\add* with all their weapons¦347739 of¦347739 war¦347741, and¦347742 with their¦347745 swords¦347745 placed under¦347746 their¦347747 heads¦347747 and¦347748 their iniquities¦347749 over their¦347749 bones¦347752, because¦347753 they were the terror¦347755 of¦347755 warriors¦347756 in¦347757 the land¦347757 of the¦347758 living¦347758.
\p
\v 28 \add ≈So¦347760\add* you, \add Mitsrayim\add* \add !(Egypt)\add*, will¦347763 be¦347763 broken¦347763 amongst the uncircumcised¦347762. You'll¦347764 lie¦347764 alongside those¦347767 who were pierced by the sword¦347769.
\p
\v 29 Edom¦347772 is \add also\add* there with its¦347773 kings¦347773 and¦347774 all¦347774 its¦347776 leaders¦347776. \add ≈Despite their strength¦347780\add*, they've¦347779 been¦347779 placed¦347779 with¦347781 those¦347783 killed¦347783 by the sword¦347785. They¦347786 lie¦347790 there along with¦347787 the uncircumcised¦347789—with those¦347793 who've gone¦347793 down¦347793 into the¦347794 pit¦347794.
\p
\v 30 All the¦347798 northern¦347798 leaders¦347797 are there, along with all the¦347802 Tsidonim¦347802 \add !(Sidonians¦347802)\add* who¦347803 went¦347805 down¦347805 with¦347806 the ones who'd been pierced. They¦347812 were¦347812 powerful¦347811 and¦347813 made others afraid, but \add now\add* they're¦347813 there in shame—uncircumcised¦347814 along with¦347815 those¦347817 who were pierced by the sword¦347819. They¦347820 carry¦347820 their¦347821 own shame, together with¦347822 the ones going¦347824 down¦347824 into the¦347825 pit¦347825.
\p
\v 31 Par'oh¦347829 \add !(Pharaoh¦347829)\add* will¦347828 look¦347828 and¦347830 be¦347830 comforted¦347830 about all¦347833 his¦347835 \add #multitudes¦347835\add* who were pierced by the sword¦347839—Par'oh¦347840 and¦347841 all¦347841 his¦347843 army¦347843. That's the¦347844 master¦347845 Yahweh's¦347846 declaration¦347844.
\p
\v 32 \add ≈Yes,\add* I¦347850 put¦347850 him there as my¦347853 \add ≈agent to terrify¦347853 those\add* in¦347855 the land¦347855 of the¦347856 living¦347856, but Par'oh¦347865 and¦347857 all¦347866 his \add #multitudes¦347868\add* will¦347857 be¦347857 laid¦347857 down among the¦347858 uncircumcised¦347859—among those¦347862 pierced by the sword¦347864. That's the¦347870 master¦347871 Yahweh's¦347872 declaration¦347870.”
\c 33
\ms1 The promise of God of his people
\mr (33:1–37:27)
\s1 Yehezkel as Yisrael's watchman
\rem /s1 Ezekiel as Israel's Watchman; God Appoints Ezekiel as a Lookout; The watchman prepares for the restored kingdom; Ezekiel Israel's Sentry; Ezekiel a Watchman
\r (Eze. 3:16-21)
\p
\v 1 Then¦347875 Yahweh¦347878 \add ≈gave\add* me¦347879 \add another\add* message¦347876:
\v 2 “Son¦347882 of¦347882 humanity¦347884, tell¦347885 this to¦347886 your¦347890 people¦347890: ‘When¦347891 I¦347896 \add ≈send¦347896 an army\add* against any \add ≈country\add*, then¦347899 the¦347900 people¦347900 of¦347900 that \add ≈country¦347902 choose¦347899 one¦347904 of¦347905 their¦347905 men¦347903 to¦347908 become\add* a¦347909 watchman¦347909 for them.
\v 3 He¦347911 looks¦347911 for \add ≈any attacker coming¦347915 onto\add* the¦347918 land¦347918, and¦347919 then he¦347919 blows¦347919 \add &his¦347919\add* horn¦347920 to warn¦347921 the¦347924 people¦347924.
\v 4 If the¦347927 people hear¦347927 the¦347930 sound¦347930 of¦347930 the¦347931 horn¦347931 but¦347932 don't¦347932 \add ≈take¦347933 any notice\add*, and¦347934 if the¦347935 \add ≈attacker\add* comes¦347934 and¦347936 kills them, then each one's¦347927 blood¦347937 is on¦347938 their own¦347938 head¦347938.
\v 5 \add Yes,\add* if someone heard¦347944 the horn¦347943 \add ≈but¦347945 paid no attention\add*, \add @that¦347946 person's¦347946\add* blood¦347947 is¦347949 on¦347948 them, \add ≈but¦347950\add* if \add @those people\add* \add ≈do pay attention\add*, they'll save¦347953 their own \add #lives¦347952\add*.
\v 6 \add ≈However,\add* if the¦347955 watchman¦347955 sees¦347958 the¦347961 \add ≈attacker\add* coming¦347962, \add ≈but¦347963\add* doesn't blow¦347965 the horn¦347966, \add ≈that is, if\add* the¦347967 people¦347967 weren't warned¦347970, and¦347971 if the¦347972 \add ≈attacker approaches\add* and¦347973 takes¦347973 anyone's¦347975 life, then that person \add ≈dies\add* in¦347977 their own sin, \add ≈but¦347979\add* I'll¦347983 require¦347983 their blood¦347979 from¦347980 the¦347982 watchman¦347982.’
\p
\v 7 Now, \add ≈talking to\add* you¦347986, son¦347987 of¦347987 humanity¦347989: I've¦347991 made you a¦347990 watchman¦347990 for¦347992 the¦347992 \add ≈Israeli¦347993 people\add*. You'll¦347994 hear¦347994 the words¦347996 from¦347995 my¦347995 mouth¦347995 and¦347997 then warn¦347997 them¦347998 on my behalf.
\v 8 If I say¦348001 to¦348002 a wicked¦348003 \add >person\add*, ‘You¦348005 wicked person, you're certainly about to die¦348005,’ and¦348006 if you¦348007 don't¦348006 announce it so as to¦348008 warn¦348008 that wicked¦348009 \add person\add* about their behaviour¦348010, then that¦348011 wicked¦348012 \add person\add* will¦348014 die¦348014 in their sin, but¦348015 \add ≈it'll be you that I¦348017 hold responsible for their death\add*.
\v 9 \add ≈But¦348019\add* if¦348020 you¦348022 warn¦348022 the¦348023 wicked¦348023 \add >person\add* about their behaviour, so that they might turn¦348025 back¦348025 from¦348026 it¦348026, and¦348027 if that person doesn't turn¦348029 back¦348029 from¦348030 their behaviour¦348030, then they'll die¦348033 in their sin, but¦348034 you yourself will have¦348036 saved¦348036 your own life¦348035.
\s1 Each person is responsible for their own actions
\rem /s1 Individual Responsibility; The Watchman's Message; God's Justice and Mercy
\p
\v 10 \add ≈So¦348039,\add* son¦348040 of¦348040 humanity¦348042, you tell¦348043 the¦348046 \add ≈Israeli¦348047 people\add*, ‘You're¦348049 saying this, “Our¦348053 errors and¦348054 our¦348054 disobedience \add ≈have¦348049 come back on¦348055 us¦348055 and they're hurting\add* us. How¦348059 can we¦348060 go on living¦348060 \add like this\add*?” ’
\v 11 Tell¦348062 them¦348063 that this is the¦348064 master¦348070 Yahweh's¦348071 declaration¦348068: ‘As I live, I don't delight¦348074 in¦348075 the¦348075 death¦348075 of¦348075 wicked¦348076 \add >people\add*. If they turn¦348080 away from¦348082 their wicked behaviour¦348082, then¦348083 they'll live¦348083! \add ≈So turn¦348084 back¦348084\add*, \add yes\add* turn¦348085 away from¦348086 your¦348086 wicked¦348087 behaviour. Why should you¦348089 \add ≈Israeli¦348091 people\add* die¦348089?’
\p
\v 12 \add ≈So¦348094 now\add*, son¦348095 of¦348095 humanity¦348097, you tell¦348098 your¦348103 people¦348103, ‘Righteous¦348104 people's righteousness¦348105 won't¦348106 save¦348107 them if they sin. Wicked¦348110 people's wickedness¦348111 won't¦348112 \add ≈cause them to die\add* if they turn¦348117 away from¦348118 their sin. \add ≈No,\add* the righteous¦348119 \add >person\add* won't¦348120 be¦348121 able¦348121 to¦348122 live¦348122 because of his righteousness if he sins¦348125.
\v 13 If I say¦348127 that a righteous person will¦348130 surely live¦348130, and¦348131 if they trust¦348133 in their righteousness¦348136 and¦348137 then commit injustice, I won't¦348143 \add ≈call to mind\add* any of \add ≈the good things they¦348144 did¦348148\add*—that person will¦348150 die¦348150 for the wickedness they committed.
\v 14 \add ≈Again,\add* if I say¦348152 to¦348153 the wicked, “You¦348155 will¦348155 surely¦348154 die¦348155,” but if they then turn¦348156 away from¦348157 their \add #sins¦348157\add* and¦348158 do¦348158 what's just and¦348160 \add ≈right¦348160\add*,
\v 15 \add ≈like\add* returning¦348163 loan guarantees that were wickedly¦348164 demanded, or \add ≈like\add* making restitution for what they've stolen, and then if they \add ≈obey the¦348167 instructions¦348167\add* that give life¦348168 and no longer \add ≈disobey\add*, then \add @those formerly wicked people\add* will¦348174 surely live¦348174—they won't¦348175 die¦348176.
\v 16 None of¦348178 the sins¦348180 that¦348182 they've¦348185 committed will¦348185 be¦348185 \add ≈called to¦348186 mind\add* against them. Those who've acted justly and¦348188 \add ≈rightly¦348188\add*, will certainly¦348190 live.
\p
\v 17 But¦348193 your¦348195 people¦348195 say¦348193, “The¦348198 master's¦348199 way¦348201 isn't¦348202 fair!” but it's¦348204 your ways that aren't fair.
\v 18 When¦348206 the righteous¦348208 \add >person\add* turns¦348206 away from¦348209 \add ≈doing¦348210 what's right¦348209\add* and¦348210 \add ≈becomes disobedient\add*, then¦348212 they'll die¦348212 in¦348213 \add @their sin\add*.
\v 19 When¦348215 the wicked¦348216 \add >person\add* turns¦348215 away from¦348217 \add ≈doing evil¦348217\add* and¦348218 does¦348218 what's just and¦348220 \add ≈right¦348220\add*, they'll live¦348223 because of those things.
\v 20 \add ≈Yes,\add* you¦348225 people say¦348225, “The¦348228 master's¦348229 way¦348231 isn't¦348226 fair!” \add but\add* I'll¦348232 judge¦348232 each of you \add ≈Israeli¦348235 people\add* according¦348231 to¦348231 \add ≈your behaviour\add*.”
\s1 The demolition of Yerushalem
\rem /s1 Explanation of Jerusalem's Fall; The News of Jerusalem's Fall; The Fall of Jerusalem; Jerusalem's Fall Explained
\p
\v 21 In¦348239 \add ≈mid-January\add* of¦348239 the twelfth year¦348241 of our¦348245 captivity \add in Bavel\add* \add !(Babylon)\add*, \add ≈someone who'd escaped¦348249\add* from¦348250 Yerushalem¦348250 \add !(Jerusalem¦348250)\add* came¦348246 to¦348251 me and told¦348251 me that the¦348253 city¦348253 had¦348252 been¦348252 captured.\x + \xo 33:21: \xt 2Ki 25:3-10; Jer 39:2-8; 52:4-14.\x*
\v 22 Yahweh¦348257 had¦348258 \add ≈held me¦348259 in¦348260 a vision\add* the evening¦348260 before¦348261 the¦348263 fugitive¦348263 came¦348262, \add ≈but¦348264\add* my mouth was opened by the time he¦348264 came¦348270 to¦348271 me¦348271 at dawn¦348272, \add ≈so¦348273 by then¦348275, I¦348276 was¦348276 able to speak again¦348277\add*.
\s1 More desolation to come
