\v 31 \add ≈So¦348454\add* my people will come¦348454 to¦348455 you¦348455, as¦348456 they often do, and will sit¦348459 in front¦348460 of¦348461 you and¦348462 listen¦348462 to your words, but¦348466 they won't¦348467 obey them. The right words are¦348474 \add ≈on their lips¦348472\add*, but their¦348477 \add #hearts¦348477\add* are¦348478 going¦348478 after¦348475 unjust¦348476 profit¦348476.
\v 32 \add ≈Yes,\add* you're¦348480 like¦348482 a¦348482 lovely song¦348482 to them, a beautiful¦348484 sound¦348485 that's¦348486 played¦348487 well¦348486 on a stringed instrument, so¦348488 they'll¦348488 listen¦348488 to your¦348491 words¦348491, but none of¦348491 them will¦348492 obey them¦348494.
\v 33 \add ≈So¦348496\add* when¦348496 all that happens, watch out, \add because it will indeed\add* happen. Then¦348499 they'll¦348499 \add ≈realise¦348499\add* that¦348500 a¦348501 prophet's¦348501 been¦348502 among¦348503 them¦348503.”
\c 34
\s1 The ‘shepherds’ of Yisrael (Israel)
