\p
\v 1 Then¦348506 Yahweh¦348509 \add ≈gave\add* me¦348510 \add another\add* message¦348507:
\v 2 “Son¦348513 of¦348513 humanity¦348515, prophesy¦348516 against Yisrael's¦348520 \add !(Israel¦348520)\add* shepherds. Prophesy¦348521 and¦348522 tell¦348522 them¦348523 that the master¦348529 Yahweh¦348530 says¦348527 this to¦348531 the¦348532 shepherds¦348532: Yisrael's¦348534 shepherds who¦348535 are¦348536 shepherding¦348537 themselves¦348538 \add ≈won't end well\add*. Shouldn't shepherds guard the¦348540 flock¦348540?
\v 3 You¦348547 eat¦348547 the¦348552 \add ≈best sheep¦348552 meat\add* and dress in \add ≈woollen¦348550 clothes¦348551\add*. You¦348553 slaughter¦348553 the¦348554 \add ≈fat lambs\add*. You¦348556 don't¦348555 shepherd¦348556 at all.
\v 4 You¦348576 haven't \add ≈taken¦348576 care of those\add* with diseases, nor do you¦348568 heal¦348568 those who are ill. You¦348571 don't bandage¦348571 up¦348571 the¦348574 ones \add ≈with broken limbs\add*, and¦348577 you don't restore the¦348579 outcasts or \add ≈search¦348581 for those who've gone missing\add*. Instead, you¦348581 use strength¦348562 and¦348582 violence to¦348569 rule¦348583 over them¦348584.
\v 5 Then¦348587 they¦348587 were¦348587 scattered¦348587 without a¦348589 shepherd¦348589,\x + \xo 34:5: \xt Num 27:17; 1Ki 22:17; Mat 9:36; Mrk 6:34.\x* and¦348590 after they were scattered, they became¦348590 food¦348591 for all¦348592 the¦348594 \add ≈wild animals¦348594\add* in the¦348595 countryside¦348595.
\v 6 My flock has strayed¦348598 across all¦348600 the¦348602 mountains¦348602 and¦348603 onto every¦348604 high¦348607 hill¦348606, and¦348608 it's dispersed over¦348608 the¦348611 entire surface¦348611 of¦348611 the¦348612 earth¦348612, yet no one¦348616 is¦348617 searching¦348616 for them.
\p
\v 7 Therefore, you shepherds¦348621, listen¦348622 to Yahweh's¦348626 message¦348625 \add to you\add*:
\v 8 This is the master¦348633 Yahweh's¦348634 declaration¦348631: As I \add ≈live¦348628\add*, my¦348630 flock¦348641 has¦348639 become¦348639 plunder and¦348644 food¦348646 for all¦348647 the¦348649 wild \add #animals¦348649\add* in the¦348650 countryside¦348650, because¦348651 there¦348651 wasn't any shepherd¦348652 and¦348653 \add ≡because¦348651\add* none of my shepherds \add ≈tried to find any of\add* my flock \add that had gotten lost\add*. \add ≈Instead it was themselves that\add* the¦348661 shepherds¦348661 \add ≈looked after\add*, and¦348663 they¦348667 didn't shepherd¦348667 my flock.
\v 9 Therefore, \add you so-called\add* ‘shepherds¦348671’, listen¦348672 to Yahweh's¦348675 message¦348673:
\v 10 The master¦348680 Yahweh¦348681 says¦348679 this: Listen, I'm¦348682 against¦348683 those shepherds¦348685. I'll¦348686 require \add ≈compensation from them for\add* my flock, and¦348691 then I'll¦348691 dismiss them¦348691 from¦348692 shepherding¦348692 the flock¦348693. Those shepherds¦348696 won't shepherd¦348698 themselves¦348699 any longer \add either\add*, \add ≈because\add* I'll¦348700 take my flock away from¦348702 their¦348702 \add #mouths¦348702\add*, so¦348703 that my flock won't¦348703 become¦348705 food¦348707 for¦348706 them¦348706 any longer.
\s1 The evil shepherds
\rem /s1 God, the True Shepherd; The Good Shepherd
\p
\v 11 \add ≈So¦348711\add* the master¦348713 Yahweh¦348714 says¦348712 this: Listen, I myself will¦348718 search¦348718 for¦348718 \add those lost from\add* my¦348721 flock¦348721, and¦348722 I¦348722 \add ≡myself\add* will¦348722 \add ≈look¦348722 after\add* them¦348722,
\v 12 like¦348724 a¦348725 shepherd¦348725 searches for his¦348726 sheep¦348732 when he's¦348729 among¦348730 his¦348732 scattered flock¦348732. So¦348734 I'll¦348735 look¦348735 for my¦348738 flock and¦348739 I'll¦348739 rescue¦348739 them¦348740 from¦348741 all¦348741 the¦348743 places¦348743 where¦348744 they¦348745 were¦348745 scattered¦348745 \add ≈during¦348747 the dark¦348749 times\add*.
\v 13 I'll¦348751 bring¦348751 \add @my¦348751 people¦348751\add* out¦348751 from¦348752 among the¦348754 \add ≈nations¦348754\add*. I'll¦348755 gather¦348755 them¦348755 from¦348756 \add foreign\add* lands¦348758 and¦348759 bring¦348759 them¦348759 \add back\add* to¦348760 their¦348762 land. I'll¦348763 put them¦348763 in pastures on Yisrael's¦348767 \add !(Israel¦348767)\add* mountainsides¦348766, by the streams, and¦348769 in¦348769 every¦348769 settlement in the¦348771 land¦348771.
\v 14 I'll¦348776 put them in¦348773 good¦348775 pastures—Yisrael's¦348781 high¦348779 mountains will¦348782 be¦348782 their¦348783 grazing places. They'll¦348785 lie¦348785 down¦348785 there¦348784 in¦348786 places good¦348787 for grazing, in abundant pastures, and¦348788 they'll¦348790 graze¦348790 on Yisrael's¦348794 hills.
\v 15 I myself will¦348797 shepherd¦348797 my¦348798 flock¦348798, and¦348799 I myself will¦348800 \add ≈give them¦348800 rest¦348800\add*. That's the¦348801 master¦348802 Yahweh's¦348803 declaration¦348801.
\p
\v 16 I'll¦348808 search¦348808 out the¦348811 lost¦348807 and¦348813 restore the¦348813 outcast. I'll¦348814 bandage¦348814 up¦348814 those who are broken and¦348815 heal those \add >who are\add* sick¦348817, but I'll¦348818 destroy¦348825 those \add >who are\add* fat¦348821 and¦348822 well. I¦348826 will¦348826 shepherd¦348826 with¦348827 justice¦348827.
\p
\v 17 \add ≈So¦348829\add* now this is what the master¦348833 Yahweh¦348834 says¦348832, You, my¦348830 flock¦348830, listen, I'll¦348835 be¦348836 a judge¦348836 between¦348837 one sheep¦348839 and¦348840 another, and¦348841 between rams¦348841 and¦348842 billy goats¦348842.
\v 18 \add ^Isn't it enough\add* to feed on the¦348847 good¦348847 pasture¦348850? Do you¦348851 have to trample¦348851 down \add ≈any remaining grass\add*? Or drink¦348856 from \add ≈clear¦348853\add* waters¦348855, then¦348857 muddy¦348860 the streams with¦348859 your feet?
\v 19 Must my¦348862 flock¦348862 eat what you've trampled¦348863 and¦348866 drink¦348868 what you've muddied with your¦348867 feet¦348867?
\p
\v 20 Therefore the master¦348874 Yahweh¦348875 says¦348873 this to¦348876 them¦348876: Listen, I myself will¦348880 judge¦348880 between¦348881 the fat¦348884 sheep and the thin¦348887 ones,
\v 21 because¦348889 you¦348892 \add shepherds\add* have pushed¦348892 them with¦348890 \add &your\add* \add #sides¦348890\add* and¦348891 \add #shoulders¦348891\add*, and¦348893 you've¦348894 gored¦348894 all¦348895 the¦348897 weak¦348897 ones with your¦348893 horns¦348893 until¦348898 you¦348900 \add succeeded in\add* scattering¦348900 them¦348901 away from the¦348904 land.
\v 22 I'll¦348906 save¦348906 my¦348907 flock¦348907 and¦348908 they'll¦348910 no longer be \add taken as\add* plunder, and¦348913 I'll¦348913 judge¦348913 between¦348914 one sheep¦348915 and¦348916 \add ≈the next\add*.
\v 23 I'll¦348918 set one¦348921 shepherd¦348922 over¦348919 them¦348923—my¦348925 servant¦348925 David¦348926. He'll¦348928 \add ≈look after\add* them¦348929, and¦348930 he'll¦348932 be their shepherd¦348934.\x + \xo 34:23: \xt Rev 7:17.\x*
\v 24 Then¦348936 I¦348936, Yahweh¦348937, will¦348938 be their god¦348940, and¦348941 my¦348941 servant¦348941 David¦348942 will¦348943 be¦348943 a leader¦348943 among¦348944 them¦348944.\x + \xo 34:24: \xt Eze 37:24.\x* I¦348945, Yahweh¦348946, have¦348947 declared that.
\rem /s1 The Lord's Covenant of Peace
\p
\v 25 Then¦348949 I'll¦348949 make¦348949 a¦348951 peace¦348952 treaty¦348951 with them and¦348953 remove the wild¦348956 animals¦348954 from¦348957 the¦348959 land¦348959, so¦348960 that they'll¦348960 \add be able to\add* live¦348960 \add ≈securely¦348962\add* in¦348961 the wilderness¦348961 and¦348963 sleep¦348963 safely in¦348964 the forests¦348964.
\p
\v 26 I'll¦348966 also \add ≈bless\add* \add both\add* them¦348967 and¦348968 the places around¦348968 my¦348969 hill¦348969, and¦348971 send¦348971 out showers in the¦348972 right season¦348973—they'll¦348976 be showers of¦348974 blessing¦348975.
\v 27 Then¦348978 the¦348979 trees¦348979 in the¦348980 countryside¦348980 will produce their fruit¦348983, the¦348984 soil will¦348985 yield its produce, and¦348987 my sheep \add ≈will¦348987 be¦348987 secure¦348991\add* in their¦348990 land¦348990. When¦348992 I¦348995 break¦348997 \add ≈off the ties holding the yoke¦349001\add* \add onto their necks\add*, and¦349002 when I¦349002 rescue¦349002 them¦349002 from¦349003 the¦349003 \add ≈control\add* of¦349003 those¦349004 who¦349004 enslaved them¦349005, then they'll¦348992 know¦348992 that¦348993 I am¦348996 Yahweh¦348996.
\v 28 They'll¦349009 no longer be¦349009 plunder¦349011 for¦349012 the \add other\add* nations¦349012, and¦349013 the¦349013 wild animals¦349013 on the¦349014 land¦349014 will¦349016 no longer devour¦349016 them¦349016. Then¦349017 they'll¦349017 live¦349017 \add ≈securely¦349018\add*, and¦349019 no one¦349020 will \add ≈make them afraid\add*.
\v 29 I'll¦349022 provide a¦349024 land for¦349023 them¦349023 that's known for¦349025 its crops, so¦349026 they¦349028 won't be¦349028 victims of¦349030 famine¦349031, and¦349033 they¦349035 won't be \add ≈mocked by\add* \add other\add* nations¦349038.
\v 30 Then¦349040 they'll¦349040 know¦349040 that¦349041 I¦349042, Yahweh¦349043 their¦349044 god¦349044, am with¦349045 them¦349045. The \add ≈Israeli¦349049 people¦349047\add* are¦349047 my¦349047 people. That's the master¦349051 Yahweh's¦349052 declaration¦349050.
\p
\v 31 You¦349054 are¦349055 my¦349055 sheep, the¦349056 flock¦349056 of¦349056 my¦349057 pasture¦349057, and my¦349057 people, and I¦349060 am¦349061 your¦349061 god¦349061. That's the¦349062 master¦349063 Yahweh's¦349064 declaration¦349062.’ ”
\c 35
