\v 5 You've always been hostile to¦349118 the Israeli¦349126 people¦349124, and when they were distressed you \add ≈decided to attack them with swords¦349131\add*—at¦349132 the¦349132 time¦349132 their¦349133 punishment¦349135 was \add ≈coming to an end¦349136\add*.
\v 6 Therefore, this is the master¦349143 Yahweh's¦349144 declaration¦349142: As I \add ≈live¦349139\add*, I'll¦349148 prepare¦349148 you¦349148 for bloodshed, and¦349149 bloodshed¦349149 will¦349150 chase¦349150 after you¦349150. Since you¦349155 didn't¦349153 hate¦349155 bloodshed, bloodshed will¦349157 \add ≈come to\add* you¦349157.
\v 7 I'll¦349159 make¦349159 \add ≈Edom\add* completely \add ≈desolate\add* when I¦349166 cut¦349166 \add ≈it off¦349166 so that no one¦349168 will want to pass¦349168 through¦349168 it\add*.
\v 8 I'll¦349171 fill¦349171 its mountain¦349174 \add ranges\add* with \add >people who were\add* killed¦349175—those¦349181 killed¦349181 by the sword¦349183 will¦349184 fall¦349184 on your high hills¦349176 and¦349177 valleys¦349177 and¦349178 in all¦349178 your¦349180 streams.
