\p
\v 10 You've¦349201 said¦349201, “These two¦349204 nations¦349205 and¦349206 these two¦349208 lands¦349209 will¦349211 become mine, and¦349212 we'll¦349212 \add ≈possess¦349212\add* them,” even when¦349213 Yahweh¦349213 was there¦349214 with them.
\v 11 Therefore, this is the master¦349222 Yahweh's¦349223 declaration¦349221: As I \add ≈live¦349218\add*, I'll¦349224 act¦349224 according¦349225 to¦349225 your¦349225 anger¦349225 and¦349226 according¦349226 to¦349226 your¦349226 jealousy¦349226 that¦349227 you¦349228 had in your hatred¦349229 of¦349229 \add @Yisrael¦349229\add* \add !(Israel¦349229)\add*, and¦349231 I'll¦349231 show myself¦349231 to them¦349232 when I¦349234 judge¦349234 you¦349234—
\v 12 then¦349236 you'll¦349236 know¦349236 that¦349237 I¦349239 am¦349240 Yahweh¦349240. I've¦349241 heard¦349241 all¦349245 the insults you¦349249 spoke¦349249 against Yisrael's¦349253 \add ≈hill¦349252 country\add*, when you said¦349254, “They've¦349256 been¦349256 destroyed—they've¦349259 been¦349259 given¦349259 over to us to devour.”
\v 13 You¦349262 raised yourselves¦349262 up against me¦349263 with¦349264 what you said, and¦349265 you¦349265 multiplied¦349265 the words¦349267 you said against me, and I heard¦349269 all of them.
\p
\v 14 The master¦349274 Yahweh¦349275 says¦349273 this: I'll¦349281 make¦349281 you¦349283 \add ≈into a desolate¦349280 place\add* while the \add ≈rest of the world cheers\add*.
\v 15 Just like you rejoiced¦349285 over the¦349286 Israeli¦349289 people's inheritance¦349286 \add ≈when it¦349293 was¦349293 made desolate¦349293\add*, I'll¦349295 do¦349295 the same to¦349297 you¦349297. You'll¦349299 become a¦349298 desolation¦349298, Mt¦349300. Se'ir¦349302 and¦349303 all¦349303 of Edom¦349305—all of¦349306 it¦349306. Then¦349307 they'll¦349307 know¦349307 that¦349308 I¦349310 am¦349311 Yahweh¦349311.”
\c 36
