\v 3 Therefore prophesy¦349347 and¦349348 tell¦349348 them that the master¦349351 Yahweh¦349352 says¦349350 this: Because¦349353 of your \add ≈desolation¦349355\add* and¦349356 because of the attacks that came on¦349356 you¦349357 from¦349358 all sides, you've¦349359 \add ≈ended up¦349363 belonging to¦349359\add* other nations¦349362—you've¦349363 been the¦349361 subject of¦349361 slanderous \add #lips¦349366\add* and¦349363 \add #tongues¦349367\add*, and¦349368 of¦349368 people's¦349370 stories.
\v 4 Therefore, mountains¦349373 of¦349373 Yisrael¦349374, listen¦349375 to the¦349376 message¦349376 from the master¦349378 Yahweh¦349379: The master¦349383 Yahweh¦349384 says¦349382 this to¦349385 the mountains¦349385 and¦349386 the high hills¦349386, to¦349387 the streambeds and¦349388 valleys¦349388, to¦349389 the \add ≈places¦349389 that have been destroyed and are now uninhabited¦349390\add*, and¦349391 to¦349391 the¦349392 forsaken¦349392 cities¦349391 that¦349393 have¦349394 become¦349394 plunder¦349395 and¦349396 a subject of¦349397 mocking for the¦349398 other nations¦349398 that¦349399 surround them—
\v 5 the master¦349407 Yahweh¦349408 says¦349406 this: I've¦349414 certainly spoken¦349414 in¦349412 the¦349412 \add ≈heat\add* of my¦349413 anger against the other nations¦349418, against Edom¦349421 and everyone¦349422 who took my land for¦349430 themselves as a¦349431 possession¦349431—against all¦349433 those who had both celebration in \add &their\add* heart¦349435 and disdain¦349436 in their spirit as they seized my land so¦349438 they could claim its¦349439 \add #pasturelands¦349439\add* for themselves.’
\p
\v 6 Therefore, prophesy¦349443 to Yisrael¦349447 and¦349448 tell¦349448 the mountains¦349449 and¦349450 the high hills¦349450, the streambeds and¦349452 the valleys¦349452, that the master¦349457 Yahweh¦349458 says¦349455 this: Listen, in¦349460 my¦349460 fury and¦349461 in¦349461 my¦349461 anger I'm¦349462 declaring this because¦349463 you've¦349466 endured¦349466 insults¦349464 from \add other\add* nations¦349465.
\v 7 Therefore, the master¦349471 Yahweh¦349472 says¦349470 this: I myself will \add ≈take action and promise\add* that the¦349481 nations¦349481 that¦349482 surround you¦349483 will¦349488 certainly \add be made to\add* carry¦349488 their own shame.
\v 8 But¦349490 you¦349490 Israeli mountains¦349491, you'll grow branches¦349493 and¦349495 bear¦349496 fruit¦349495 for¦349497 my¦349497 Israeli¦349498 people¦349497, since¦349499 they'll¦349500 soon come¦349500 back to¦349501 you,
\v 9 because¦349503, listen, I'm¦349504 for you¦349505, and¦349506 I'll¦349506 treat you¦349507 favourably—you'll¦349508 be¦349508 ploughed and¦349509 sown¦349509 \add with seed\add*.
\v 10 I'll¦349511 multiply¦349511 \add ≈your population—all¦349514 the¦349516 Israeli¦349517 people\add*. The¦349520 cities¦349520 will¦349519 be¦349519 inhabited¦349519 \add again\add* and¦349521 the¦349521 ruins¦349521 rebuilt¦349522.
\v 11 I'll¦349524 increase¦349528 \add both\add* people and¦349524 animals¦349527 on¦349525 you¦349525 \add ≡mountains\add* so that they'll¦349528 multiply¦349528 and¦349529 be¦349529 fruitful¦349529. Then¦349530 I'll¦349530 cause¦349530 you to¦349530 be¦349530 inhabited¦349530 like¦349532 you were previously, and¦349533 I'll¦349533 make you prosper more¦349534 than¦349534 you did in the past \add ≈so¦349535 that\add* you'll¦349535 know¦349535 that¦349536 I¦349538 am¦349539 Yahweh¦349539.
\v 12 I'll¦349541 bring my¦349546 Israeli¦349547 people¦349546 to¦349541 walk¦349541 on¦349542 you¦349542. They'll¦349548 possess¦349548 you¦349548, and¦349549 you'll¦349549 be their inheritance¦349551, and¦349552 you'll¦349554 no longer \add ≈cause¦349541 their children to¦349556 die\add*.
\p
\v 13 The master¦349561 Yahweh¦349562 says¦349564 this: They're telling you¦349565, “You¦349568 \add ≡mountains\add* devour¦349566 people¦349564, bereaving¦349570 your \add #nation¦349571\add* of¦349571 children,”
\v 14 therefore you¦349579 won't consume¦349579 people any longer, and¦349581 you'll¦349584 no longer make your¦349581 \add #nation¦349581\add* mourn their deaths. That's the¦349588 master¦349589 Yahweh's¦349590 declaration¦349588.
\v 15 I¦349594 won't allow you to hear¦349594 the¦349597 insults¦349597 from the¦349598 \add other\add* nations¦349598 any longer—you'll no longer have to bear¦349602 the¦349599 people¦349600 groups shaming you¦349602, and¦349605 you¦349609 won't cause¦349609 your nation to¦349609 stumble¦349609. That's the¦349611 master¦349612 Yahweh's¦349613 declaration¦349611.”
\rem /s1 The Renewal of Israel; Israel's New Life
\p
\v 16 Then¦349616 Yahweh¦349619 \add ≈gave\add* me¦349620 \add another\add* message¦349617:
\v 17 “Son¦349623 of¦349623 humanity¦349625, when the¦349626 \add ≈Israeli¦349627 people\add* inhabited¦349628 their¦349631 land¦349631, they¦349632 defiled¦349632 it¦349633 with their¦349634 customs and¦349635 their activities. \add ≈In my eyes,\add* their customs were like¦349636 the¦349636 uncleanness¦349636 of¦349636 a woman's menstruation¦349637,
\v 18 \add ≈so¦349642\add* I¦349642 poured¦349642 out¦349642 my¦349643 fury¦349643 against them¦349644 for the¦349647 blood¦349647 that¦349648 they'd¦349650 poured¦349650 out¦349650 on¦349651 the¦349653 land¦349653, and¦349654 for how they'd¦349655 polluted it¦349655 with their¦349654 idols¦349654.
\v 19 I¦349657 scattered¦349657 them¦349658 among¦349659 the nations¦349659—they¦349660 were¦349660 dispersed¦349660 through the lands¦349661. I¦349664 judged¦349664 them according¦349662 to¦349662 their¦349662 customs and¦349663 their¦349663 actions¦349663.
\v 20 Then¦349666 they went¦349666 to¦349667 those \add other\add* nations¦349669, and wherever¦349670 they¦349672 went¦349672, they¦349674 profaned¦349674 my holy name¦349677 when¦349679 people asked¦349679 about them¦349680, ‘Are¦349681 these¦349684 \add really\add* Yahweh's¦349683 people? After all, they've¦349686 been thrown out¦349686 of¦349685 his¦349685 land¦349685.’
\v 21 \add ≈But¦349688\add* I¦349688 had compassion for my holy name¦349691 that¦349693 the¦349695 \add ≈Israeli¦349696 people\add* had defiled¦349694 among¦349697 the \add other\add* nations¦349697, when they¦349700 went¦349700 there.
\p
\v 22 Therefore tell¦349705 the¦349706 \add ≈Israeli¦349708 people\add* that the master¦349711 Yahweh¦349712 says¦349710 this: I'm not¦349713 doing this for¦349714 the sake¦349714 of¦349717 you \add ≈Israeli¦349718 people\add*, but for¦349722 my¦349724 \add ≈sacred¦349724\add* name¦349722, which¦349725 you've¦349726 profaned¦349726 among¦349727 the nations¦349727 everywhere you've¦349730 gone¦349730.
\v 23 My¦349736 great¦349737 name¦349736, which¦349738 you \add people\add* have¦349738 profaned¦349738 among the nations, I'll¦349733 make holy¦349733 \add even\add* among¦349739 the nations¦349739 \add where\add* you¦349741 profaned¦349741 it. Then¦349743 the¦349744 nations¦349744 will¦349743 know¦349743 that¦349745 I¦349747 am¦349748 Yahweh¦349748, when¦349752 they see you recognise my \add ≈holiness\add*. That's the master¦349750 Yahweh's¦349751 declaration¦349749.
\v 24 I'll¦349756 take¦349756 you¦349757 \add back\add* out of those nations¦349760 and¦349761 gather¦349761 you¦349762 from¦349763 every¦349763 land¦349765, and¦349766 I'll¦349766 bring¦349766 you¦349767 into¦349768 your¦349770 land.
\v 25 Then¦349772 I'll¦349772 sprinkle¦349772 pure water¦349774 on¦349773 you¦349773 so¦349776 you'll¦349776 be¦349776 cleaned from¦349777 all¦349777 of¦349778 your¦349778 impurities¦349778, and¦349779 I'll¦349782 purify¦349782 you from¦349779 all¦349779 your¦349781 idols¦349781.
\v 26 I'll¦349785 give¦349785 you¦349786 \add people\add* a¦349787 new heart and a new spirit¦349789 in¦349792 your¦349792 innermost¦349792 parts, and¦349793 I'll¦349793 take¦349793 the¦349796 stony heart¦349796 away from¦349798 your¦349798 \add ≈bodies\add* and¦349799 \add ≈replace it with\add* a¦349801 heart¦349801 of¦349801 flesh¦349802.\x + \xo 36:26-28: \xt Eze 11:19-20.\x*
\v 27 I'll¦349807 put¦349807 my¦349806 spirit¦349806 in¦349808 you and¦349809 enable you¦349814 \add Israelis\add* to \add ≈follow¦349814 my instructions and keep¦349816 my regulations¦349813\add*.
\v 28 Then¦349819 you'll¦349819 inhabit¦349819 the¦349820 land¦349820 that¦349821 I¦349822 gave¦349822 to¦349823 your¦349823 ancestors¦349823—you'll¦349824 be¦349824 my people¦349826 and¦349827 I'll¦349828 be your god¦349830.
\v 29 I'll¦349832 save¦349832 you¦349833 from¦349834 all¦349834 of¦349835 your¦349835 uncleanness¦349835, and¦349836 then I'll¦349836 summon¦349836 the¦349839 grain¦349839 and¦349840 multiply¦349840 it¦349841—I'll¦349844 no longer \add ≈assign\add* famine¦349846 to¦349845 you¦349845.
\v 30 I'll¦349848 multiply¦349848 the¦349851 \add #fruit¦349851 on the¦349852 trees¦349852\add* and¦349853 the¦349853 produce¦349853 \add ≈from the¦349854 soil\add* so¦349855 that you'll no longer \add ≈be shamed by other nations¦349862 seeing you¦349858 suffering\add* famine¦349861.
\v 31 Then¦349864 you'll¦349864 think¦349864 about¦349864 your¦349867 wicked¦349868 customs¦349867 and¦349869 your¦349869 activities that¦349870 weren't good¦349873, and¦349874 \add ≈your faces¦349875 will display your loathing¦349874 of¦349877 your¦349877 own sins and¦349878 your¦349879 disgusting habits\add*.
\v 32 But make sure you know¦349889 this: I'm not¦349881 doing all that for¦349882 \em your¦349882\em* sake¦349882, \add ≈so you¦349890 Israeli¦349895 people\add* should be¦349891 ashamed¦349891 and¦349892 disgraced because of¦349893 your¦349893 \add ≈behaviour¦349893\add*. That's the master¦349887 Yahweh's¦349888 declaration¦349886.
\p
\v 33 The master¦349900 Yahweh¦349901 says¦349899 this: \add ≈When\add* I¦349903 purify¦349903 you¦349904 from¦349905 all¦349905 your¦349906 disobedience, I'll¦349907 enable you to¦349907 inhabit¦349907 the¦349910 cities¦349910 \add again\add* and¦349911 to rebuild¦349911 the¦349912 ruined¦349912 places¦349912,
\v 34 and¦349914 the¦349914 idle land¦349914 will¦349916 be¦349916 tilled¦349916 until it's¦349919 no longer a¦349920 wasteland¦349920 for everyone¦349924 to¦349921 see as they go¦349924 past.
\v 35 Then¦349926 \add instead\add* they'll say¦349926, “This¦349928 land¦349927 was desolate¦349929, but it's¦349930 become¦349930 like¦349931 the¦349931 garden¦349931 of¦349931 Eden¦349933—the¦349934 abandoned cities¦349934 and the uninhabited ruins that were torn¦349937 down¦349937 are now fortified¦349938 and inhabited.”
\v 36 Then¦349941 the¦349942 other nations¦349942 around¦349945 you¦349945 will¦349941 know¦349941 that¦349946 I¦349948 am¦349944 Yahweh¦349949, because¦349946 I¦349950 built¦349950 up the¦349951 ruins and replanted the¦349953 abandoned¦349953 places¦349953. I¦349954, Yahweh¦349955, have¦349956 declared it and¦349957 I¦349957 will¦349957 do¦349957 it.
\p
\v 37 The master¦349962 Yahweh¦349963 \add also\add* says¦349961 this¦349965: The¦349967 \add ≈Israeli¦349969 people\add* will again¦349964 ask me to do¦349970 this for¦349971 them¦349971: to increase¦349972 \add ≈their population like¦349974 sheep¦349974\add*.
\v 38 Just like¦349977 the flock¦349977 \add ≈that's kept separate to be used\add* for sacrifices (like¦349979 the¦349979 flock¦349979 in Yerushalem¦349980 \add !(Jerusalem¦349980)\add* at¦349981 its¦349981 scheduled feasts), so¦349982 too the¦349985 ruined¦349985 cities¦349984 will be filled with flocks¦349987 of¦349987 people and¦349989 they¦349989 will¦349989 know¦349989 that¦349990 I¦349992 am¦349993 Yahweh¦349993.”
\c 37
\s1 The valley with bleached bones
\rem /s1 A Valley of Dry Bones; The Valley of Dry Bones
\p
\v 1 \add ≈One day Yahweh¦350000 gave me another vision\add*, and¦350001 he¦350001 took¦350001 me¦350001 out¦350001 by¦350002 \add *his\add* spirit¦350002 and¦350004 put¦350004 me¦350004 down¦350004 in¦350005 the¦350005 middle¦350005 of¦350006 a valley¦350006 that was¦350008 full¦350008 of bones¦350009.
\v 2 Then¦350011 he¦350011 led me¦350011 all around¦350011 them¦350012, and¦350016 wow¦350016, there were so many¦350017 bones¦350017 in the¦350022 valley¦350022, and¦350023 they¦350024 were¦350024 totally dried¦350024 out!
\v 3 “Son¦350029 of¦350029 humanity¦350031,” he \add ≈asked\add* me, “can these¦350034 bones¦350033 become living¦350032 \add people\add* again?”
\p “My¦350036 master¦350036 Yahweh¦350037,” I \add ≈replied\add*, “\add ≈only you would know¦350039 that\add*.”
\p
\v 4 Then¦350041 he¦350041 told¦350041 me¦350042, “Prophesy¦350043 over these¦350047 bones and¦350048 tell¦350048 them¦350049, ‘Dry¦350051 bones. Listen¦350052 to Yahweh's¦350055 message¦350053.
\v 5 The master¦350059 Yahweh¦350060 says¦350058 this to¦350061 these¦350062 bones¦350061: Listen, I'm¦350064 about¦350065 to¦350065 put breath¦350067 into¦350066 you¦350066, and¦350068 you'll¦350068 live¦350068.
\v 6 I'll¦350070 \add ≈connect\add* sinews to¦350071 you¦350071 and¦350073 put flesh¦350075 onto you. I'll¦350076 cover¦350076 you¦350077 with skin¦350078 and¦350079 put¦350079 breath¦350081 into¦350080 you¦350080 so¦350082 you'll¦350082 live¦350082. Then¦350083 you'll¦350083 know¦350083 that¦350084 I¦350086 am¦350087 Yahweh¦350087.’ ”
\p
\v 7 \add ≈So¦350089\add* I¦350089 prophesied¦350089 as¦350090 I¦350091 was¦350091 instructed¦350091, and¦350092 wow¦350096, a¦350094 sound¦350094 like¦350095 something rattling¦350098 started as the¦350100 bones¦350100 moved together—bone¦350101 against bone¦350104!
\v 8 I¦350106 looked¦350106 and¦350107, wow¦350107, the bones now had sinews on¦350109 them¦350109, and¦350111 flesh¦350111 grew up¦350112 \add over that\add*, and¦350113 then skin¦350115 covered¦350113 them¦350114! \add ≈But¦350117\add* there¦350118 was¦350118 \add still\add* no breath in¦350119 them¦350119.
\p
\v 9 Then¦350121 \add @Yahweh¦350121\add* told¦350121 me¦350122, “Prophesy¦350123 to¦350124 the¦350126 wind¦350143, son¦350128 of¦350128 humanity¦350130, prophesy and¦350131 tell¦350131 the air, ‘The master¦350140 Yahweh¦350141 \add ≈commands\add* this: Breath, come from¦350142 the four¦350142 \add ≈compass points\add*, and¦350146 breathe into these¦350148 who've been killed¦350147, so¦350149 they'll¦350149 \add ≈come to life¦350149\add*.’ ”
\p
\v 10 \add ≈So¦350151\add* I¦350151 prophesied¦350151 just¦350152 like¦350152 I was commanded¦350153. Then¦350154 breath¦350156 came¦350154 into¦350155 them¦350155 and¦350157 they¦350157 \add ≈came to life¦350157\add*. Then¦350158 they¦350158 stood¦350158 on¦350159 their¦350161 feet¦350161—a very large¦350163 army¦350162.
\p
\v 11 Then¦350169 \add @Yahweh¦350169\add* \add ≈informed\add* me¦350170, “Son¦350171 of¦350171 humanity¦350173, these¦350175 bones are¦350176 the¦350178 entire¦350176 \add ≈Israeli¦350179 population\add*. Listen, they're¦350180 saying¦350182, ‘Our bones have¦350183 dried¦350183 up¦350183 and¦350185 our¦350186 hope¦350186 is gone. We've¦350187 been¦350187 cut¦350187 off¦350187.’
\v 12 Therefore prophesy¦350191 and¦350192 tell¦350192 them¦350193, ‘The master¦350197 Yahweh¦350198 says¦350196 this: Listen, I'll¦350200 open¦350201 your graves and¦350205 lift¦350205 you¦350206, my¦350208 people¦350208, out from them, then¦350209 I'll¦350209 bring¦350209 you¦350210 back to¦350211 Yisrael¦350214 \add !(Israel¦350214)\add*.
\v 13 ⇔Then, my¦350229 people¦350229, when I open¦350222 your graves and¦350226 bring¦350226 you out of them, you'll¦350217 know¦350217 that¦350218 I¦350220 am¦350221 Yahweh¦350221.
\v 14 I'll¦350231 place¦350231 my¦350232 spirit¦350232 within you¦350233 so¦350234 you'll¦350234 live¦350234, and¦350235 I'll¦350235 cause you¦350236 to rest in your¦350239 land¦350239 when¦350240 you¦350240 know¦350240 that¦350241 I¦350243 am Yahweh¦350244. I¦350245 declare it, and¦350246 I¦350246 will¦350246 do¦350246 it. That is Yahweh's¦350249 declaration¦350247.’ ”
\s1 The two sticks indicating unity of Yisrael and Yehudah
\rem /s1 One Nation Under One King; The Two Sticks; Reunion of Israel and Judah; Judah and Israel in One Kingdom
\p
\v 15 Then¦350252 Yahweh¦350255 \add ≈gave\add* me¦350256 \add another\add* message¦350253:
\v 16 “\add ≈So¦350259 now\add*, son¦350260 of¦350260 humanity¦350262, take¦350263 a stick for¦350265 yourself¦350265 and¦350268 write¦350268 on¦350269 it¦350269, ‘For¦350270 Yehudah¦350270 \add !(Judah¦350270)\add* and¦350271 for¦350271 all their associated people¦350271.’ Then¦350275 take¦350275 another stick¦350276 and¦350278 write¦350278 on¦350279 it¦350279, ‘For¦350280 \add Yisrael\add* \add !(Israel)\add* (\add represented by\add* Yosef¦350280 \add !(Joseph¦350280)\add*, the¦350281 branch of¦350281 Efrayim¦350282 \add !(Ephraim¦350282)\add*), and¦350283 for all¦350283 their associated people.’
\v 17 Then¦350290 hold both of them¦350291 together so that they \add ≈seem like\add* one stick¦350297 in¦350301 your¦350301 hand¦350301.
\v 18 When¦350303 your¦350307 people¦350307 \add ≈ask¦350308 you and insist\add*, ‘Aren't¦350309 you¦350311 going to tell¦350311 us¦350312 what¦350313 these¦350315 props of yours mean?’
\v 19 then tell¦350318 them¦350319, ‘The master¦350323 Yahweh¦350324 says¦350322 this: Look, I'm¦350326 taking¦350327 Yosef's¦350331 branch that's¦350332 in¦350333 Efrayim's¦350335 hand along with the¦350336 tribes¦350336 of¦350336 Yisrael¦350337 his companions¦350338, and¦350340 joining it¦350342 to Yehudah's¦350346 branch, so¦350347 that¦350332 they'll make¦350347 one¦350349 branch, and¦350350 they'll¦350350 become one¦350351 in¦350352 my hand.’
\p
\v 20 Hold the¦350355 branches in¦350360 your¦350360 hand¦350360 that¦350356 you¦350358 wrote¦350358 on¦350359 \add ≈while they¦350354 watched\add*.
\v 21 Tell¦350363 \add @the¦350364 people¦350364\add*, ‘The master¦350368 Yahweh¦350369 says¦350367 this: Look, I'm¦350371 about¦350372 to¦350372 take¦350372 the¦350375 Israeli¦350376 people¦350375 out from¦350377 the¦350378 nations¦350378 where¦350379 they¦350380 went¦350380. I'll¦350383 gather¦350383 them¦350384 from¦350385 the surrounding¦350385 lands and¦350386 bring¦350386 them¦350387 \add back\add* to¦350388 their¦350390 land¦350390.
\v 22 I'll¦350392 \add ≈unite them¦350393 as a¦350394 single\add* nation¦350394 in the¦350396 land¦350396, on¦350397 the¦350397 mountains¦350397 of¦350397 Yisrael¦350398, and¦350399 there'll be one king as king over all¦350402 of them¦350402, and¦350404 they'll¦350405 no longer be two¦350409 nations¦350410—they'll¦350412 no longer be¦350412 divided¦350412 into¦350414 two¦350414 kingdoms¦350415.
\v 23 Then¦350418 they'll¦350419 no longer defile¦350419 themselves¦350419 with their¦350421 idols¦350421, with their¦350422 disgusting things, or with any of their¦350424 other sins. I'll¦350425 save¦350425 them¦350426 from¦350427 all¦350427 of¦350428 their¦350428 faithless actions\f + \fr 37:23 \ft The Hebrew text has ‘living places’ rather than ‘faithless actions’ (from the Septuagint), but it's difficult to make sense of the Hebrew.\f* with which¦350429 they've¦350430 sinned¦350430, and¦350432 I'll¦350432 purify¦350432 them¦350433 so¦350434 they'll¦350434 be¦350434 my people¦350437 and¦350438 I'll¦350439 be their god¦350441.
\v 24 My¦350443 servant¦350443 David¦350444 will¦350445 be¦350445 king¦350445 over¦350446 them¦350446, \add ≈so¦350447\add* there'll be one¦350448 shepherd¦350447 over them all¦350450,\x + \xo 37:24: \xt Eze 34:24.\x* and¦350451 they'll¦350452 \add ≈follow¦350452\add* my instructions and keep¦350454 my¦350453 regulations¦350453 and¦350455 obey them¦350456.
\v 25 They'll¦350458 live¦350458 in the¦350461 land¦350461 that¦350462 I've¦350463 given¦350463 to¦350464 my servant Ya'akov¦350465 \add !(Jacob¦350465)\add* \add (also called Yisrael)\add*, where your¦350470 ancestors¦350470 had stayed. They'll¦350467 live¦350467 in¦350469 it¦350469 forever¦350484—they, their children, and their¦350476 grandchildren¦350475, and¦350480 my servant David¦350480 will¦350482 be¦350482 their \add ≈permanent\add* leader¦350482.
\v 26 I'll¦350486 establish a¦350488 peace¦350489 treaty with them—a¦350490 never-ending agreement¦350490 with them¦350493. I'll¦350494 establish them¦350494 and¦350495 multiply¦350495 them¦350496 and¦350497 put¦350497 my¦350500 sacred place among¦350501 them¦350501 forever¦350502.
\v 27 My¦350505 residence¦350505 will be with¦350506 them¦350506—I'll¦350507 be¦350507 their god¦350509, and¦350510 they'll¦350511 be my people¦350514.\x + \xo 37:27: \xt 2Cor 6:16; Rev 21:3.\x*
\v 28 Then¦350516 the¦350517 \add other\add* nations¦350517 will¦350516 know¦350516 that¦350518 I¦350519 am¦350521 Yahweh¦350520 who sets Yisrael¦350524 apart, when¦350525 my¦350526 sacred place is¦350525 \add ≈permanently\add* among¦350527 them¦350527.’ ”
\c 38
\ms1 The defeat of all of Yisrael's opponents
\mr (38:1–39:29)
\s1 Invasion by Gog and his army
\rem /s1 Gog as the Instrument of God; A Message for Gog; A Prophecy Against Gog; Invasion by Gog
\p
\v 1 Then¦350531 Yahweh¦350534 \add ≈gave\add* me¦350535 \add another\add* message¦350532:
\v 2 “Son¦350538 of¦350538 humanity¦350540, \add ≈look\add* toward the¦350546 land¦350546 of¦350546 Magog¦350547 \add ?where King\add* Gog¦350545 is the¦350548 main leader¦350548 of¦350549 Meshek¦350550 and¦350551 Tuval¦350551,\x + \xo 38:2: \xt Rev 20:8.\x* and¦350552 prophesy¦350552 against¦350543 him¦350553.
\v 3 Tell¦350555 him that the master¦350558 Yahweh¦350559 says¦350557 this: Listen, I'm¦350560 against¦350561 you¦350561, Gog¦350562, leader¦350563 of¦350564 Meshek¦350565 and¦350566 Tuval¦350566,
\v 4 \add ≈so¦350568\add* I'll¦350568 turn¦350568 you¦350568 around¦350568 and¦350569 put¦350569 hooks¦350570 into¦350571 your¦350571 jaws¦350571. Then¦350572 I'll¦350572 bring¦350572 you out¦350572 with all¦350577 your¦350579 army¦350579, horses¦350580, and¦350581 horsemen¦350581, all of¦350584 them¦350584 dressed¦350582 in full armour—a¦350585 huge group¦350585 with large¦350586 and¦350588 small shields¦350588, all of them holding swords¦350590.
\v 5 Paras¦350593 \add !(Persia¦350593)\add*, \add Kush\add* \add !(Ethiopia)\add* (Kush¦350594), and¦350595 Libya are with¦350596 them¦350596, all¦350597 of¦350597 them¦350597 with \add #shields¦350598\add* and¦350599 \add #helmets¦350599\add*,
\v 6 \add as well as\add* Gomer¦350601 and¦350602 all¦350602 its troops, and Beyt-Togarmah¦350606, from the¦350607 far parts¦350607 of¦350607 the¦350608 north¦350608, and¦350609 all¦350611 its troops. Many¦350615 people¦350614 groups are¦350616 with¦350616 you¦350616.
\v 7 \add Tell Gog to\add* \add ≈get¦350627 ready¦350618 as commander, and¦350619 to¦350620 assemble¦350625 and prepare¦350619 his troops\add*.
\v 8 You'll¦350633 be¦350633 \add ≈summoned¦350633 many days¦350631 later\add*, then after some years¦350635 you'll¦350636 go¦350636 to¦350638 a¦350640 land¦350640 that's recovered from¦350643 war and \add ≈where the¦350643 people have come back from¦350645 many¦350646 nations\add*—gathered¦350644 back to Yisrael's¦350649 \add !(Israel¦350649)\add* mountains¦350648 that¦350650 had¦350652 continuously¦350654 been a¦350653 ruin. But¦350655 the land's people¦350656 will \add indeed\add* be¦350657 brought¦350657 out¦350657 of the nations, and¦350658 they'll¦350658 all¦350660 live¦350658 \add there\add* safely \add again\add*.
\v 9 Then¦350662 you'll¦350662 go¦350662 \add ≈in like¦350663 a storm¦350663 with your large army\add*—you'll¦350664 all¦350670 be like¦350665 a cloud¦350665 covering¦350666 the¦350667 land¦350667.
\p
\v 10 The master¦350680 Yahweh¦350681 says¦350679 this: \add But\add* \add #plans\add* will \add start to\add* form in¦350684 your¦350690 heart¦350690 on that¦350685 day¦350684 and¦350691 you'll¦350691 devise wicked¦350693 schemes.
\v 11 Then¦350695 you'll¦350695 \add ≈think\add*, ‘I'll¦350696 \add take my army\add* up¦350696 onto the open ground¦350699—\add ≈we'll attack\add* the people living quietly \add ≈and peacefully¦350702\add*—all¦350705 of them¦350705 living¦350706 where there¦350711 are¦350706 no \add #walls¦350708\add* or barriers, and no city gates¦350710.
\v 12 I'll capture¦350716 booty and steal plunder \add ≈and¦350716 use my forces\add* against those ruins¦350722 that have been newly inhabited¦350723, and¦350724 against those people¦350726 who've returned from¦350728 the nations¦350728—people who are gaining¦350729 livestock¦350730 and¦350731 property¦350731, and who¦350732 are living¦350732 at¦350733 the¦350735 centre¦350735 of¦350735 the¦350736 world¦350736.’
\v 13 \add People from\add* Sheva¦350738 and¦350739 Dedan¦350739, and¦350740 traders¦350740 from Tarshish¦350741 and¦350742 its¦350744 villages will¦350745 \add ≈ask¦350745\add* you, ‘Have you come¦350750 to¦350751 plunder? Have¦350753 you¦350753 assembled¦350753 your¦350754 armies to¦350755 take¦350755 away¦350755 spoil, to carry¦350755 off gold¦350758 and silver¦350757, to¦350759 take¦350759 \add &their\add* livestock¦350760 and¦350761 property¦350761 and to¦350762 haul away plenty of plunder?’
\p
\v 14 Therefore, son¦350769 of¦350769 humanity¦350771, prophesy¦350768 and¦350772 tell¦350772 Gog¦350773 that the master¦350776 Yahweh¦350777 says¦350775 this: On that day¦350780, when¦350782 my¦350783 people¦350783 Yisrael¦350784 are living¦350782 \add ≈securely¦350785\add*—\add ≈but you¦350786 won't¦350778 take notice of that¦350781\add*—
\v 15 you'll¦350788 come¦350788 from¦350789 your¦350789 place¦350789 far away in the¦350791 north¦350791 with¦350795 a large¦350800 army¦350801—all¦350798 of them riding¦350796 on horses¦350797, \add yes,\add* \add ≈a¦350799 very numerous force\add*.
\v 16 Then¦350804 you'll¦350804 attack my¦350807 \add ≈Israeli¦350808 people¦350807\add* like¦350809 a cloud¦350809 that covers¦350810 the¦350811 land¦350811. I'll¦350815 send¦350815 you¦350815 against my¦350818 land¦350818 \add ≈near the end¦350812 of¦350818 the era\add*, so¦350819 that the¦350821 nations¦350821 might know¦350820 me¦350822 when¦350823 I¦350823 show¦350823 myself¦350823 through you¦350824, Gog¦350826—\add ≈they'll see with their own eyes¦350825 that I always demand what's right\add*.
\rem /s1 Judgment on Gog
\v 17 The master¦350832 Yahweh¦350833 says¦350831 this: \add ^Aren't\add* you¦350834 the one that I¦350839 spoke¦350839 about in¦350840 the¦350842 past \add ≈through¦350842\add* my¦350843 servants¦350843, the¦350844 Israeli¦350845 prophets¦350844 who¦350846 prophesied¦350846 for years¦350849 in their own times, that I would bring¦350850 you¦350851 against them¦350852?
