\p
\v 1 In¦351509 \add ≈mid-April\add* of the twenty-fifth year¦351511 of¦351512 our¦351512 captivity (the fourteenth year after¦351520 \add @Yerushalem\add* \add !(Jerusalem)\add* was captured), Yahweh¦351532 \add ≈used his power to¦351535 take\add* me there,
\v 2 \add yes,\add* God¦351538 took¦351539 me¦351539 to¦351540 Yisrael¦351543 \add !(Israel¦351543)\add* in¦351537 visions¦351537. He¦351544 put¦351544 me¦351544 on a¦351547 very¦351549 high¦351548 mountain¦351547 \add where\add* there seemed to be¦351550 city¦351553 buildings towards the¦351554 south¦351554,\x + \xo 40:2: \xt Rev 21:10.\x*
\v 3 and¦351556 he¦351556 took¦351556 me¦351557 there. Then¦351559 wow¦351559, there was a¦351561 man¦351561 standing¦351572 in¦351573 the \add city\add* gateway¦351573 who \add ≈looked like¦351563\add* bronze¦351564! \add ≈He was holding\add* a¦351565 linen¦351567 cord¦351565 and¦351569 a \add ≈measuring¦351570\add* rod.\x + \xo 40:3: \xt Rev 11:1; 21:15.\x*
\p
\v 4 The¦351577 man¦351577 told¦351598 me, “Son¦351578 of¦351578 humanity¦351580, look¦351581 with¦351582 your¦351582 eyes¦351582 and¦351583 listen¦351584 with¦351583 your¦351583 ears¦351583, and¦351585 fix¦351585 your¦351586 \add ≈mind¦351586\add* on everything¦351587 that¦351588 I'm¦351590 revealing to¦351591 you¦351592, because¦351593 you¦351596 were¦351596 brought¦351596 here so¦351594 I could reveal them to¦351595 you¦351595. Report¦351598 everything you¦351605 see¦351606 \add here\add* to¦351607 the¦351607 \add ≈Israeli¦351608 people\add*.”
\s1 The eastern gateway
\rem /s1 The East Gateway; The East Gate to the Outer Court; The East Gate
\p
\v 5 There was a¦351611 wall¦351611 surrounding the¦351612 temple¦351613 area. The \add ≈measuring\add* rod in¦351617 the¦351618 man's¦351618 hand was \add ≈just over three metres long\add*. (It was¦351621 six¦351621 long cubits¦351623—each long cubit was a cubit long plus¦351625 a¦351625 handbreadth.) \add ≈So¦351626\add* he¦351626 measured¦351626 the¦351629 wall, and it was one¦351632 measuring rod thick and¦351633 one¦351635 high¦351633.\x + \xo 40:5–42:20: \xt 1Ki 6:1-38; 2Ch 3:1-9.\x*
\v 6 Then¦351637 he¦351637 went¦351637 to¦351638 the¦351640 \add temple\add* gate¦351640 that¦351641 faced¦351642 east¦351644. He¦351645 went up its¦351646 steps¦351646 and¦351648 measured¦351648 the gate's¦351653 threshold¦351658—one rod across.
\v 7 The¦351664 guard chambers¦351664 were each one¦351666 rod \add ≈long¦351667 and¦351668 deep, and¦351671 just under three metres¦351674 wide¦351670\add*. The temple gate threshold¦351675 by¦351677 the¦351678 temple porch¦351678 was one¦351682 rod across.
\v 8 He¦351684 measured¦351684 the¦351687 porch¦351687 inside the¦351688 gate¦351688 and it was one¦351691 rod long,
\v 9 and¦351693 the¦351696 porch¦351696 over the¦351697 gate¦351697 was one rod deep. The doorposts were \add each\add* a metre wide. (This was the¦351704 porch¦351704 at the¦351705 gate¦351705 facing the¦351706 temple¦351706.)
\v 10 There were three guard chambers¦351708 on either side of¦351708 the¦351709 east¦351711 gate¦351709, and each of¦351710 them \add ≈was the same size\add*, and¦351714 the¦351718 walls that separated them¦351718 \add ≈were the same size\add*.
\p
\v 11 Then¦351725 the man measured¦351725 the¦351728 width¦351728 of¦351728 the¦351729 gateway entrance¦351729 \add ≈and it was five metres¦351733\add*, and the¦351734 length¦351734 of¦351734 the¦351735 gateway entrance \add ≈was almost seven metres¦351738\add*.
\v 12 He measured the wall that \add ≈ran along\add* the front¦351741 of¦351741 the¦351742 chambers¦351742 at half a metre high. The¦351750 chambers¦351750 measured three metres on each side.
\v 13 Then¦351759 he¦351759 measured¦351759 the¦351762 gateway¦351762 from¦351763 the¦351763 roof¦351763 of¦351764 one chamber to that of the next chamber, \add ≈and¦351768 it was thirteen metres¦351769\add* from the entrance of the first chamber to that of the second.
\v 14 Then¦351774 he¦351774 measured the¦351782 wall that went between the¦351783 guard chambers, \add ≈and it was over thirty metres long\add* as far as the¦351784 gate's¦351784 porch.
\v 15 The¦351792 entrance¦351792 from the front¦351790 of¦351790 the¦351791 gate¦351791 to¦351796 the¦351796 other end of¦351796 the¦351797 gate's porch¦351797 was twenty-seven metres.
\v 16 There were closed¦351804 windows facing the¦351807 chambers¦351807 and¦351808 toward their¦351809 pillars¦351809 within¦351810 the \add #gates¦351811\add* all around, and¦351815 likewise for the porches¦351816. There were windows all around the inside¦351821, and¦351822 each of the door jambs was decorated with \add carvings of\add* palm¦351825 trees¦351825.
