\p
\v 17 Then¦351827 the man brought¦351827 me¦351827 to¦351828 the¦351831 outer¦351831 courtyard \add of the temple\add*. Look¦351832, there were rooms¦351833, and¦351834 the courtyard¦351836 \add ≈was paved\add*, with thirty¦351840 rooms¦351841 next to¦351842 the¦351844 pavement¦351844.
\v 18 The¦351846 pavement¦351846 \add ≈reached\add* to¦351847 the¦351849 side¦351849 of¦351849 the¦351850 gates¦351850, and its width was the¦351852 same as the¦351853 gates'¦351853 length¦351852. That was the¦351855 lower¦351855 pavement.
\v 19 Then¦351857 the man measured¦351857 the¦351858 distance from¦351859 the front of the¦351861 lower¦351861 gate to¦351862 the¦351862 front¦351862 of¦351862 the¦351864 inner¦351864 gate: it was \add ≈just over fifty metres\add* on the¦351868 eastern¦351868 side, and¦351869 the same on the northern¦351869 side.
