\p
\v 20 ⇔Then¦351871 he¦351878 measured¦351878 the length¦351879 and¦351880 width¦351880 of the¦351871 gate¦351871 that¦351872 was¦351874 at the northern¦351875 \add end\add* of the¦351877 outer¦351877 courtyard¦351876.
\v 21 There were three chambers¦351882 on each side of¦351882 that gate, and¦351886 the gate with its¦351888 \add #porch¦351890\add* \add ≈measured¦351893\add* the¦351893 same as the¦351894 main gate¦351894: \add ≈twenty-seven metres long¦351898 and¦351899 thirteen metres wide¦351899\add*.
\v 22 Its¦351904 windows¦351904, porch¦351906, chambers, and¦351908 its¦351908 palm¦351908 trees¦351908 matched the eastern¦351915 gate¦351911. Seven¦351917 steps¦351916 went¦351918 up¦351918 to it¦351920 and¦351921 to its¦351921 porch.
\v 23 There was a¦351925 gate¦351925 to¦351926 the¦351927 inner¦351927 courtyard¦351926 \add ≈in¦351928 front¦351928 of¦351928\add* the¦351929 northern¦351930 gate¦351929, just as there was at the eastern¦351931 gate. The man measured¦351932 from¦351933 one gate¦351933 to¦351934 the other gate¦351936, \add ≈and it was fifty-four metres\add*.
\s1 The southern gateway
