\p
\v 32 Then¦352072 the man brought¦352072 me¦352072 to¦352073 the¦352076 inner¦352076 courtyard¦352075 by the eastern¦352078 side and¦352079 measured¦352079 the¦352082 gate¦352082, which had the¦352083 same measurements¦352083 as the¦352084 other gates.
\v 33 Its¦352086 chambers¦352086, walls, and¦352088 porches¦352090 \add ≈measured¦352092\add* the¦352092 same as the¦352093 other gates, and¦352094 there were windows¦352094 all around. The¦352101 inner gate with its porch \add ≈was¦352102 twenty-seven metres long¦352101 and¦352104 thirteen metres wide¦352104\add*.
\v 34 Its¦352109 \add #porch¦352109\add* \add that\add* faced the¦352112 outer¦352112 courtyard¦352111 had \add carved\add* palm¦352113 trees¦352113 on each side of¦352116 it, and eight¦352120 steps¦352121 going up it.
