\p
\v 35 Next the man brought¦352125 me¦352125 to¦352126 the¦352128 northern¦352129 gate¦352128 and¦352130 measured it, \add and\add* it measured the¦352131 same as the¦352132 other gates.
\v 36 Its¦352134 chambers¦352134, walls, and¦352138 porch measured the same as the other gates, and¦352140 there were windows¦352140 all around. The¦352145 gateway with its porch \add ≈was¦352146 twenty-seven metres long¦352145 and¦352148 thirteen metres wide¦352148\add*.
\v 37 Its¦352153 porch \add that\add* faced the¦352156 outer¦352156 courtyard¦352155 had \add carved\add* palm¦352157 trees¦352157 on each side of¦352160 it, and eight¦352164 steps¦352165 going up it.
\s1 Rooms for preparing sacrifices
