\p
\v 38 There¦352173 was a¦352169 room¦352169 with a door¦352170 by each of¦352170 the¦352172 inner gateways¦352172 which was where they rinsed¦352174 the¦352177 burnt¦352177 \add #offerings¦352177\add*.
\v 39 There were¦352179 two¦352181 tables¦352182 on each side of each porch¦352179, which were for slaughtering¦352187 \add the offerings:\add* the¦352189 burnt¦352189 offering¦352189, the¦352190 sin¦352190 offering¦352190, and¦352191 the¦352191 guilt¦352191 offering¦352191.
\v 40 By the wall of the courtyard, going¦352197 up¦352197 to¦352198 the¦352199 gate¦352199 to the¦352200 north¦352200, there were two¦352201 tables¦352202. Also¦352203 on the¦352206 other¦352206 side there were¦352208 two¦352210 tables¦352211 at the¦352208 gate's porch¦352208.
\v 41 There¦352215 were four¦352216 tables¦352217 by the¦352220 gate¦352220 on each side¦352219—they slaughtered¦352224 animals on those eight¦352221 tables¦352222.
\v 42 There were four¦352226 cut-stone tables¦352227 for¦352228 the¦352231 burnt offerings, \add ≈each just under a metre long¦352231 and wide¦352235, and¦352238 standing half¦352238 a¦352240 metre tall\add*. They kept the¦352246 tools which¦352247 they used to slaughter¦352248 the¦352251 burnt¦352251 offerings¦352251 for the¦352253 \add #sacrifices¦352253\add* on those \add stone\add* tables.
\v 43 Some two-pronged hooks¦352255 a¦352256 handbreadth in length were¦352258 fastened all around in the porch, and¦352263 the¦352266 flesh¦352266 of¦352266 the¦352267 \add #offerings¦352267\add* would be put on the¦352265 tables¦352265.
\s1 The priests' rooms
\rem /s1 Rooms for the Priests
\p
\v 44 Within the¦352271 inner¦352271 courtyard¦352274 \add but\add* on the¦352269 outside¦352269 of¦352279 the¦352280 inner gate¦352280 were singers'¦352273 rooms¦352272—one¦352285 on the¦352281 northern¦352281 side facing south¦352284, and¦352282 the¦352283 other on the¦352284 southern¦352284 side¦352288 facing¦352291 north¦352293.
\v 45 Then¦352295 the man told¦352295 me¦352296, “This¦352297 room¦352298 facing¦352300 south¦352302 is¦352303 for¦352303 the priests¦352303 who¦352304 are on duty in the temple¦352306.
\v 46 The¦352308 room¦352308 facing¦352310 north¦352312 is¦352313 for¦352313 the priests¦352313 on duty at the¦352316 altar¦352316, that¦352309 is¦352318, for Tsadok's¦352320 descendants—they're the¦352321 \add only\add* Levites who¦352314 approach¦352321 Yahweh¦352327 to¦352328 serve¦352328 him¦352328.”
\s1 The inner courtyard
\rem /s1 The Inner Courtyard and the Temple Building; The Inner Courtyard and Temple
\p
\v 47 Next he¦352330 measured¦352330 the¦352333 square¦352341 courtyard¦352333 at fifty-four metres long¦352334 and¦352338 wide¦352338, with the¦352342 altar¦352342 in¦352343 front¦352343 of¦352343 the¦352344 temple¦352344.
